\par\par \b \uc2 TREASURIES-U.S. bonds slip in Europe\b0\par\par\uc2 538 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 August 2011\par 12:35\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Becalmed Italian and Spanish debt markets dull demand for Treasuries\par \par \uc2 * Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  proceeds seen supporting U.S. bonds\par \par \uc2 * Two-/10-year Treasuries curve still seen flatter\par \par \uc2 By Emelia Sithole-Matarise\par \par \uc2 LONDON, Aug 4 (Reuters) - U.S. Treasuries fell in European trade on Thursday as lower-rated euro zone government bonds stabilised on hopes the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will resume its bond purchase programme to combat a sharp selloff in Italian and Spanish bonds.\par \par \uc2 U.S. stock index futures pointed to a firmer start on Wall Street with Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken the yen showing resolve among central banks to fight stronger \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  compounding the impact from a global slowdown.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to push back against the yen strength came less than 24 hours after the Swiss \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  slashed rates to combat a stronger \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The surge in the yen and franc had made life difficult for economies grappling with deflation or little inflation, showing the strongest response yet from central banks dealing with the fallout of the U.S. troubles and euro zone debt crisis.\par \par \uc2 Demand for safe-haven Treasuries and German Bunds cooled as Italian and Spanish bond yields retreated from 14-year highs on speculation that the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will revive bond purchases in the secondary market after a 4-month hiatus.\par \par \uc2 Decent demand at a Spanish bond auction added to a stabler mood before the ECB policy decision later in the day.\par \par \uc2 "What's driving the market now is that European peripherals are doing well so both Bunds and Treasuries are under pressure," Craig Collins, a trader at \uc2 Bank of Montreal\uc2  in London said.\par \par \uc2 "People are expecting (ECB President Jean-Claude) Trichet is going to be talking about ECB buying European debt to try and assuage fears."\par \par \uc2 September T-note futures <TYv1> fell 13/64 to 126-27/32, from a nine-month peak of 127-23/64 touched the previous day.\par \par \uc2 Technical gauges are signalling the contract is starting to look overbought, with the relative strength index on the daily chart now around 70. An RSI above 70 implies overbought conditions while below 30 implies an oversold market.\par \par \uc2 "We're at levels in Treasuries where there is a natural reactive correction," said Marc Ostwald, a strategist at Monument Securities.\par \par \uc2 Benchmark 10-year T-note yielded 2.615 percent, retreating from a nine-month low of 2.546 percent reached the previous day. Since the shock downward revisions to U.S. GDP last Friday, 10-year yields have slid about 30 bps.\par \par \uc2 Treasuries fell despite \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's hefty \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  -- estimated by traders at roughly 1 trillion yen ($12.8 billion) during the Asian trading day.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  has historically bought Treasuries with \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  proceeds and, unlike other major central banks with hefty reserves, keeps most of its foreign assets concentrated in dollars.\par \par \uc2 The two-/10-year curve stabilised around 228 bps, still about 25 bps flatter over the past week, reflecting the reduced expectations for future growth and inflation. Collins at \uc2 Bank of Montreal\uc2  says it could push to 220 bps -- a level last reached a year ago -- if the safe-haven rally resumes.\par \par \uc2 (Editing by Anna Willard)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-BONDS-TREASURIES   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020110807e7840008y\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
