\par\par \b \uc2 CEE MARKETS 1- \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  recovers after Japans move lifts mood\b0\par\par\uc2 594 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 August 2011\par 10:30\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Yield appeal of CEE \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  boosted by Japan, Swiss moves\par \par \uc2 * Mkts await Czech, ECB rate decisions\par \par \uc2 * CEE stockmarkets mixed\par \par \uc2 By Marcin Goettig\par \par \uc2 WARSAW, August 4 - Central European \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  gained slightly on Thursday, recouping some of Wednesday's losses, after \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the markets to weaken the yen, boosting the yield appeal of local \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  ahead of rate decisions in the Czech Republic and the euro zone.\par \par \uc2 A day after the \uc2 Swiss National Bank\uc2  (SNB) unexpectedly cut rates to weaken its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the yen skidded around 3 percent against the dollar on the back of repeated yen selling by Japan, which fears a stronger yen will impede its economic recovery.\par \par \uc2 Yen \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and a cut in Swiss interest rates stand to boost the appeal of Central European \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , if risk appetite improves, as interest rates in the region could still rise further this year.\par \par \uc2 "Japan followed SNB's suit and surely investors will not want to bid up now the franc and yen to such strong levels as before," a Warsaw-based \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader said.\par \par \uc2 By 0737 GMT, the Polish zloty had gained 0.2 percent to 4.021 to the euro. On Wednesday, it had lost 0.6 percent to the euro, and, along with Hungary's forint , hit all-time lows versus the Swiss franc as global growth concerns hit emerging European \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "Assuming a positive scenario, with improving sentiment on bond markets and bourses, the zloty may strengthen in the direction of 4.0 per euro," the trader added.\par \par \uc2 The zloty is supported by expectations of another Polish interest rate rise this year.\par \par \uc2 Central European stock indexes were mixed in early trade on Thursday though as investors, unnerved by weak global economic data this week, remained nervous.\par \par \uc2 The forint added 0.4 percent against the euro and the Czech crown , seen as a safe haven in the region, edged up 0.2 percent.\par \par \uc2 In a Reuters poll, 20 out of 22 analysts expect the Czech \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to keep its key two-week repurchase rate\par \par \uc2 at an all-time low of 0.75 percent.\par \par \uc2 The decision is to be announced at 1100 GMT, followed by a news conference at 1230 GMT.\par \par \uc2 Elsewhere, at 1145 GMT the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is expected to keep rates flat at 1.50 percent. Investors will be looking for any indication the ECB might resume bond purchases in the face of a deterioration in market confidence in the euro zone's ability to resolve the bloc's debt crisis. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par --------------------------MARKET SNAPSHOT-------------------- \par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2                     Latest   Previous Local    Local\par                                close \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par                                            change   change\tab \par                               today   in 2011\tab \par Czech crown       24.224   24.26   +0.15%   +3.2%\tab \par Polish zloty       4.021    4.03   +0.22%   -1.57%\tab \par Hungarian forint 271.1    272.07   +0.36%   +2.54%\tab \par Croatian kuna      7.444    7.444   0%      -0.86%\tab \par Romani