\par\par \b \uc2 Aussie, NZD dlr leap on yen as  \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervenes \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 669 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 August 2011\par 07:56\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2  * Aussie jumps 2 pct on yen, but down 1 pct vs USD\par \par \uc2  * Kiwi 1.6 pct lower vs USD\par \par \uc2  * Aussie at risk of testing $1.0560 \par \par \uc2  By Gyles Beckford and Cecile Lefort\par \par \uc2  SYDNEY/WELLINGTON, Aug 4 (Reuters) - The Australian and New Zealand dollars jumped on the yen on Thursday after Japanese authorities \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to restrain their racy \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , while the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  eased monetary policy. \par \par \uc2  However, with both the Bank of Japan and the Swiss \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  acting to lift the U.S. dollar, the Aussie took a 1 percent hit on the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to $1.0660 . Support seen at $1.0650, the 19 July trough, ahead of major barriers at $1.0560.\par \par \uc2  Against the yen, the Aussie catapulted 2 percent higher\par \par \uc2 to 84.72 yen. The cross, which broke through the 200-day MA of 84.15, is likely to find major resistance at 85.05, the 38.2 percent of the 90.04-82.03 April-August decline, ahead of the Ichimoku could base of 85.58. \par \par \uc2  Similarly, the kiwi leapt 1.5 percent to 67.44 yen with a first barrier seen at Tuesday's high of 68.10, ahead of 69.35, the trend high of May 2010.\par \par \uc2  The BOJ buying revived a U.S. dollar that had been weighed by speculation the U.S. Federal Reserve might consider another round of quantitative easing (QE).\par \par \uc2  "Japan was incredibly influential and mitigated talk of QEIII," said David Scutt, a trader at \uc2 Arab Bank Australia\uc2 .\par \par \uc2   Across the Tasman sea, investors dumped the kiwi, 1.6 percent lower, with comments by the nation's Finance Minister adding to the downward pressure.\par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  skidded a cent and a half to $0.8510 , or 1.6 percent lower with resistance seen at $0.8490.\par \par \uc2  "It was all about the BoJ, which was significant and a little surprising in terms of the timing, hence the reaction, and it was worth a cent (fall) in the kiwi," said \uc2 Westpac\uc2   senior \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist Imre Speizer.\par \par \uc2  The fall in the kiwi was given some momentum by Finance Minister Bill English who reiterated in parliament that a strong kiwi dollar was hurting exporters and activity. \par \par \uc2  He said there was no monetary policy solution to the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's level and cast doubt that \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  would likely work.\par \par \uc2  "We would prefer a lower exchange rate, the world's not delivering that to us, so we have to get on and build a competitive economy," English said. See \par \par \uc2   Markets have been speculating that the RBNZ may be the next \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 , following Switzerland's surprising easing overnight to restrain its soaring \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2  The New Zealand dollar has gained 9 percent this year.\par \par \uc2 Westpac\uc2 's Speizer said he believed the kiwi has peaked and faced possible further correction into a range of $0.8000 to $0.8400. He said short term support is around $0.8500 with $0.8650 a topside hurdle.\par \par \uc2  The Aussie bounced back against its kiwi cousin to NZ$1.2532\par \par \uc2 , having it a one-year low at NZ$1.2366 earlier in the week. The cross has fallen from about NZ$1.30 in early July.\par \par \uc2  The NZ \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was unmoved by jobs data showing the unemployment rate steady at 6.5 percent, in line with expectations. Aa meagre 1,000 jobs were added in the second quarter, although there were some signs of the labour market perking up. \par \par \uc2  This was seen leaving expectations of a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate rise next month intact. See \par \par \uc2  New Zealand government bonds <0#NZTSY=> were mixed, with the short end easing, but mid-to-late dated maturities firming by up to 4 basis points.\par \par \uc2  Australian bond futures pulled back a little after recent huge gains, with the 3-year contract <YTTc1> down 0.09 points to 95.890, and the 10-year <YTCc1> 0.07 points lower to 95.295. \par \par \uc2 (Australia/New Zealand bureaux)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-AUSTRALIA-NEWZEALAND-\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2 /BONDS   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020110807e78400046\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
