\par\par \b \uc2 Indian rupee drops on oil demand, dlr gains\b0\par\par\uc2 445 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 August 2011\par 05:59\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  pushes dollar up, hurts rupee\par \par \uc2 * Positive local shares seen limiting rupee losses\par \par \uc2 * Rupee seen in 44.30-44.45 range - traders\par \par \uc2 (Updates to mid-morning)\par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, Aug 4 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee weakened on Thursday as payments for oil imports picked up, while the dollar's rise after \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stem the yen's strength also weighed.\par \par \uc2 Refiners have been buying dollars for days to clear dues of about $5 billion to Iran. The payments had been held up for seven months after the Indian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  scrapped a clearing mechanism last December.\par \par \uc2 At 10:57 a.m. (0527 GMT), the partially convertible rupee\par \par \uc2 was at 44.4350/4400 per dollar, 0.3 percent weaker than Wednesday's close of 44.31/32.\par \par \uc2 Traders said exporters were cashing in their dollars and this should keep the rupee rangebound at 44.30-44.45 during the day.\par \par \uc2 "There is demand from oil importers, but it is met with supply from software exporters. That is why it is likely to be rangebound," a \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader with a state-run bank said.\par \par \uc2 The dollar rose above 79 yen for the first time in two weeks on Thursday as the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market intermittently to stem the yen's strength.\par \par \uc2 The index of the dollar against six major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  was up 0.7 percent at 74.562 points.\par \par \uc2 The euro was at $1.4273, compared with $1.4290 when the rupee closed on Wednesday and traders said the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  would be watched for direction.\par \par \uc2 Oil posted a modest rebound from one-month lows tracking a bounce in Asian stock markets ahead of key U.S. employment reports expected to shed further light on whether a recovery in the world's largest economy is faltering.\par \par \uc2 Indian shares were trading up 0.3 percent after falling to their lowest close in nearly six weeks in the previous session.\par \par \uc2 The one-month onshore forward premium was at 21.25 points from 22.50 on Wednesday, while the three-month was at 64.25 points from 67.75 and the one-year was at 212 points from 217.75.\par \par \uc2 One-month offshore non-deliverable forward contracts were quoted at 44.58, weaker than the onshore spot rate.\par \par \uc2 In the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  futures market , the most traded near-month dollar-rupee contracts on the National Stock Exchange was at 44.5950 while on the MCX-SX and the United Stock Exchange were at 44.5925. Total volume stood at $3.4 billion.\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Shamik Paul; Editing by Ranjit Gangadharan)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-INDIA-RUPEE/ (UPDATE 1)   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020110807e7840002d\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
