\par\par \b \uc2 INSTANT VIEW 6- \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervenes \highlight\uc2 , BOJ set to ease policy\b0\par\par\uc2 1,033 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 August 2011\par 04:09\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Aug 4 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  solo in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on Thursday to stem one-sided rises in the yen that was hurting the country's economy, while the Bank of Japan was set to ease monetary policy.  \par \par \uc2 Finance Minister Katsuhiko Noda declined to comment on whether Tokyo will continue to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and did not disclose the size of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 A trader said \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  authorities were continuing to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  sporadically in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  cut short its two-day policy meeting that was due to end on Friday. *************************************************************** \par \par \uc2  KEY POINTS\par \par \uc2  - The dollar jumped to 78.47 yen on trading platform EBS from about 77.00 yen. \par \par \uc2  - The Nikkei stock average gained 1 percent after being flat prior to the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2  COMMENTARY\par \par \uc2  OSAMU TAKASHIMA, CHIEF \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCY\b0 \highlight\uc2  STRATEGIST, CITIBANK TOKYO\par \par \uc2  "I don't think the level was an issue. There was a sense of crisis even at about 80 yen, but no particular opportunity to step in. I think they moved now because stocks have begun to fall globally."\par \par \uc2  "Basically, I don't think solo \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is effective -- they need to act in unison. But I think they will keep it up for a while, I don't think the action is over yet. The effects are sometimes seen immediately, but sometimes it's more of a long-term thing."\par \par \uc2  SACHA TIHANYI, SENIOR \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCY\b0 \highlight\uc2  STRATEGIST, SCOTIA CAPITAL IN HONG KONG\par \par \uc2  "I think that \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  will be successful only in so far as it tames strong speculative buying in the yen by putting "the fear of God" into speculative yen longs. Thus the BOJ can only hope to keep the market on edge... It is a big liquid market however, and it is always difficult to fight a trend without coordinated sustained \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ."\par \par \uc2  NAGAYUKI YAMAGISHI, STRATEGIST, MITSUBISHI UFJ MORGAN STANLEY SECURITIES\par \par \uc2  "Yesterday's monetary easing by Switzerland provided the push, because if Japan didn't respond this would push the yen still higher, since it's the yen and the Swiss franc that are really being bought these days. A response needed to be taken quickly to head off any further yen strengthening.\par \par \uc2  "But it's a solo move by Japan and we don't know the actual amount. The economic situations for the U.S., Europe and Japan are very different right now and so this makes a joint \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  pretty unlikely. We have to wait and see what happens when we move into European trading time, but the impact of the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  may be pretty limited."\par \par \uc2  HIDEO KUMANO, EXECUTIVE CHIEF ECONOMIST, DAI-ICHI LIFE RESEARCH INSTITUTE, TOKYO\par \par \uc2  "The message here is that Japan won't tolerate the yen's appreciation beyond 77 yen a dollar. Meanwhile, the Bank of Japan has decided to end its policy meeting earlier than planned on Thursday.\par \par \uc2  "It's not clear at the moment if further easing measures by the BOJ will have an immediate effect. But the fact that the government and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  are taking steps concurrently are underscoring their resolve."       \par \par \uc2  SEAN CALLOW, SENIOR \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCY\b0 \highlight\uc2  STRATEGIST, WESTPAC INSTITUTIONAL BANK, SYDNEY:\par \par \uc2  "History suggests that the BOJ action will support USD/JPY for a few days at most but won't alter the overall trend. Sept. 15, 2010 solo \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was very large scale but USD/JPY started to reverse within a matter of days." \par \par \uc2  KATSUTOSHI INADOME, FIXED-INCOME STRATEGIST, MITSUBISHI UFJ MORGAN STANLEY SECURITIES, TOKYO\par \par \uc2  "Solo \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  won't have much impact on the market. But if the United States does not oppose the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and sees a stronger dollar as a benefit, it could pave the way for a change in U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy."\par \par \uc2  "The BOJ bringing forward its monetary policy is not a surprise for the market which already expected the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to ease in some form. Japan's long-term interest rates are likely to decline backed up by such easing."\par \par \uc2  TAKASHI KAMIYA, CHIEF ECONOMIST, T&D ASSET MANAGEMENT CO\par \par \uc2  "I think the MOF wanted to stem the yen's rise, which was very rapid, particularly if we look at the effective exchange rate.\par \par \uc2  "The MOF couldn't leave the dollar at 77 yen, because soon it would've fallen to 75 yen and perhaps even below that, so they're trying to bring the dollar back up as close to 80 yen as possible.\par \par \uc2  "In terms of timing, it was really well thought through, as the BOJ stepped into the market right after the Swiss \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  embarked on monetary easing the day before.\par \par \uc2  "But the yen's advance reflects the difficult economic and fiscal situation of both the U.S. and the euro zone, so even if \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market, it won't be able to combat the yen's rise in the long run on its own."\par \par \uc2  TAKEO OKUHARA, FUND MANAGER, DAIWA SB INVESTMENTS\par \par \uc2  "The move by the \uc2 Swiss National Bank\uc2  to ease to counter the recent sharp appreciation of the Swiss franc made it easier for the Japanese government and the Bank of Japan to take steps.\par \par \uc2  "The Swiss move suggested consensus was building for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and to highlight the coordiation effectiveness, the BOJ moved forward its policy announcement to today from tomorrow.\par \par \uc2  "It is rare for the Japanese government and the BOJ to move solidly in tandem, so their coordinated action will deliver a strong message to the markets."\par \par \uc2  MAKOTO NAGAHORI, HEAD OF EQUITIES AT INSTINET\par \par \uc2  "The impact from the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  may be short-lived as the view that the yen is still a safe haven \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  hasn't changed amid concerns over the global economy.\par \par \uc2  "The government must have wanted to show that it is committed to acting promptly and appropriately before things are too late."\par \par \uc2  "While most manufacturers peg their dollar assumption rate at around 80 yen, it would be too late to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  if the dollar dips further against the yen.\par \par \uc2  "But if the closely watched U.S. unemployment confirms a stagnant recovery in the U.S. economy this Friday, the dollar will likely fall, and the yen may rise again anyway."\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Tokyo and Singapore newsrooms)\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 JAPAN\b0 \highlight\uc2 -MARKETS/\b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  (INSTANT VIEW 5)   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020110807e7840001d\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
