\par\par \b \uc2 JGBs Down As BOJ Easing Underwhelms,  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Weakens Yen\b0\par\par\uc2 436 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 August 2011\par 10:37\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global News Select\par \uc2 DJON\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par                                      At 0600 GMT   Change \par    TFX Jun 3-Mos Euroyen Price:       99.665       Unchanged \par    TSE Sep 10-Yr JGB Futures Price:   142.21       -0.02 \par    10-Yr 1.2% JGB No. 316 Yield:      1.020%       +0.010 \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 TOKYO -(Dow Jones)- Japanese government bond prices fell in Tokyo Thursday after the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Ministry of Finance intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to weaken the yen and the Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  cut short a policy board meeting to announce further easing measures that failed to impress investors expecting more aggressive steps.\f28 \par \par \uc2 The government launched a yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  in morning trade in Tokyo, sending the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  down sharply against its counterparts. The weaker yen removes some support for safe-haven JGBs, as it gives some breathing space to Japan's key export sector and buoys share prices.\par \par \uc2 The BOJ followed the MOF by increasing its six-month fixed rate purchases by Y5 trillion and asset-purchase fund by Y5 trillion. Most investors expected a move roughly of this scope.\par \par \uc2 But some market participants had recently been betting the strong yen would force the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to take more aggressive steps such as quantitative easing. When it didn't, these investors sold JGBs on the view they would likely not get much help out of the BOJ steps, analysts said.\par \par \uc2 Any further moves by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the months ahead "depend on how global financial markets and the Japanese economy develop," said Naomi Hasegawa, senior fixed income strategist at Mitsubishi UFJ Morgan Stanley Securities. "If the global financial market falls into another abyss or the Japanese economy runs out of steam, there will be pressure for the BOJ to do more."\par \par \uc2 There were signs Thursday that JGBs may have room for further gains. The yield on the 10-year JGB fell earlier to a near nine-month low at 0.995%. Yields in other maturities also touched multi-month lows.\par \par \uc2 "There are clear sources of demand for the 10 year-plus sector, such as life insurers mainly investing their funds in 10year-plus bonds and investors targeting yield decline," said Akito Fukunaga, chief rates strategist at RBS Securities Japan.\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    Other Cash Bond Yields            At 0600 GMT   Change \par    2-Year 0.2% JGB No. 306 Yield:      0.145%      Unchanged \par    5-Year 0.4% JGB No. 97 Yield:       0.350%      +0.005 \par    20-Year 1.9% JGB No. 128 Yield:     1.755%      Unchanged \par    30-Year 2.2% JGB No. 34 Yield:      1.885%      -0.025 \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Andrew Monahan, Dow Jones Newswires; 81-3-6269-2783; andrew.monahan@dowjones.com [ 08-04-11 0437ET ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1037 4153  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJON000020110804e7840002g\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw200\pich25\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3000\pichgoal375
