\par\par \b \uc2 INTERVIEW: \uc2 Moody's\uc2  Analyst: Japan Action 'Positive', Challenges Remain\b0\par\par\uc2 414 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 August 2011\par 14:58\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 -- \uc2 Moody's\uc2  analyst: \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's additional easing steps, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  'positive'\par \par \uc2 -- Impact of measures likely to be limited over time, \uc2 Tom Byrne\uc2  tells Dow Jones\par \par \uc2 -- Byrne: Japan's credit challenges: fiscal consolidation and economic growth revitalization, remain\par \par \uc2 (Adds context from eighth paragraph.)\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    By Natasha Brereton-Fukui \par    Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 SINGAPORE (Dow Jones)--New easing measures by the Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to weaken the yen are "positive actions," but their impact is likely to be limited over time and they don't remove the "big credit challenges" the country faces, a senior analyst at Moody's Investors Service said Thursday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan stepped into the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market Thursday, launching a yen-selling campaign that was backed up by Y10 trillion ($125.5 billion) in easing measures from the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , as officials said they needed to tame market speculation threatening a fragile economic recovery.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Moody's\f28 \uc2 \f2  lead sovereign analyst for Japan \f28 \uc2 \f2 Tom Byrne\f28 \uc2 \f2  told Dow Jones Newswires that the BOJ's easing would help offset deflationary pressures and, to some extent, aid the recovery of economic activity from various constraints caused by March's devastating earthquake.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 He noted that the yen's climb was becoming the No. 1 concern for exporters, now that the quake-damaged supply chain was normalizing.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "BOJ easing and MOF \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  are positive actions, although they will probably have limited effects over time," Byrne said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "However, Japan's big credit challenges remain--fiscal consolidation and economic growth revitalization," he cautioned.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Moody's\f28 \uc2 \f2  is nearing the end of a three-month assessment period on Japan's Aa2 sovereign rating, having put it on review for possible downgrade May 31.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The credit rating agency previously highlighted growing concerns that deteriorating prospects for economic growth and a weak policy response would make it harder for Japan's government to design and enact a credible roadmap for deficit reduction.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 It warned a "tipping point" could be reached at which investors would demand a risk premium to hold Japanese government debt.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's public debt amounts to twice its annual economic output---the highest ratio in the industrialized world.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 In a much awaited long-term fiscal overhaul blueprint in June, Prime Minister Naoto Kan's government bowed to political pressure and watered down a key plan to double the sales tax by March 2016.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Natasha Brereton-Fukui, Dow Jones Newswires; +65 6415 4044; natasha.brereton-fukui@dowjones.com [ 04-08-11 1258GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020110804e78400194\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
