\par\par \b \uc2 News Highlights: Top Economic Stories Of The Day\b0\par\par\uc2 716 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 August 2011\par 14:00\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par TOP STORIES \par  \par \f28 \uc2 \f2 KRAFT FOODS\f28 \uc2 \f2  TO SPLIT INTO 2 PUBLICLY TRADED COMPANIES \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Kraft Foods\f28 \uc2 \f2  intends to separate into two publicly traded companies by separating its North American grocery business from its global snacks \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , becoming the latest big corporation to announce plans to split. Shares up 3% premarket.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par RIO TINTO POSTS RECORD 1H NET, RAISES BUYBACK \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Rio Tinto\f28 \uc2 \f2 's 1H earnings surge to $7.6 billion even as it warns of sovereign-debt risk in the U.S. and Europe. The world's second-largest iron ore miner also lifts its share buyback plan to $7 billion from $5 billion.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par JAPAN ACTS TO WEAKEN YEN, BOJ EASES FURTHER \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's government launches a yen-selling campaign backed up by Y10 trillion in easing measures from the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , as officials say they need to tame market speculation threatening a fragile economic recovery.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par GREECE TO PASS WIDE-RANGING REFORM BILL, BUT FACES CHALLENGES \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Greece's parliament will pass a hastily assembled reform bill to overhaul everything from online gambling to tourism developments, but opposition to the plan is likely to create problems in pushing through ambitious reforms.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par GM PROFIT JUMPS 92% ON STRONG GLOBAL SALES \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Auto maker's 2Q earnings surge to $2.5 billion, or $1.54 a share, as revenue soars, bolstered by stronger global sales and an increase in production of high-margin pickup trucks and SUVs in North America. Analysts forecast $1.20 a share. Shares gain 2% premarket.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UNILEVER PROFIT RISES, WARNS ON WESTERN EUROPE \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Unilever\f28 \uc2 \f2  posts a rise in 1H profit on higher sales driven by volume and pricing gains in emerging markets, but the world's third-largest maker of branded household products warns that Western Europe remains challenging.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par ECB HOLDS KEY RATE AT 1.5% AS DEBT CRISIS SPREADS \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  left its benchmark interest rate unchanged at 1.5%, as expected, as a deepening debt crisis threatens stability in Italy and Spain and recent data point to weakening economic growth.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par BOE KEEPS RATES ON HOLD AS OUTLOOK DARKENS \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Bank of England keeps its key interest rate at a record low for the 30th straight month against a backdrop of slackening growth in the U.K. and gloomier prospects for the global economy.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par US STOCK FUTURES LOWER AHEAD OF JOBS DATA \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Stock futures drop as nervous investors show no appetite for extending the previous session's modest gains while awaiting the latest figures on weekly jobless claims. Kraft shares jump 8% premarket after announcing plans to split the company in two.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CRUDE FALLS OVER 1% ON BOJ \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCY INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 Crude oil futures fell over 1% to fresh lows as the Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan intervensd\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets pushing the dollar sharply higher against all major \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par  \par  \par    ======== DOW JONES NEWSWIRES ANALYSIS AND COMMENTARY ======== \par  \par Morning Briefing \par STOCK FUTURES DOWN AS JOBS DATA LOOM \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Stocks are expected to open lower, as investors adopt a cautious stance ahead of key labor market data over the next two trading sessions. A string of downbeat economic readings out of the U.S. this week has depicts a weakening recovery for the world's largest economy.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par Money Talks \par DON'T BANK ON QE3 \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Now that the U.S. economy appears to be slowing again and equities are once again taking a beating, it's natural for investors to start talking about further infusions of liquidity from the Fed. Right? Maybe not, Alen Mattich writes.\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Focus \par TIME TO COORDINATE THE UNCOORDINATED \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 First the SNB tried to push the franc down and then the BOJ opted to do the same for the yen but these moves are a far cry from the coordinated policy efforts needed to stop investors from fleeing risky markets, writes Nicholas Hastings.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par   ============ MARKETS ACTION ============ \par  \par US STOCK FUTURES DROP AHEAD OF JOBS DATA \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Stock futures are lower ahead of US jobless claims data.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par US TREASURYS DOWN AFTER \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 JAPAN INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 Treasurys down after \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 JAPAN\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  ACTS TO WEAKEN YEN, DOLLAR RISES \par  \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  continues \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to weaken yen, dollar rises.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CRUDE FALLS OVER 1% ON BOJ \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCY INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 Crude futures fall to fresh lows following BOJ's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par SPOT GOLD FLAT; MARKET SEEN CROWDED, BUT SUPPORTED \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Spot gold is flat, hovering below record highs. [ 04-08-11 1200GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1030 1804 4180   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020110804e7840016m\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
