\par\par \b \uc2 News Highlights: Top Economic Stories Of The Day\b0\par\par\uc2 607 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 August 2011\par 11:48\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 JAPAN\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  LAUNCHES \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  TO PUSH DOWN YEN, BOJ EASES FURTHER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 TOKYO (Dow Jones)--Japan stepped into the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market Thursday, launching a yen-selling campaign that was backed up by Y10 trillion in easing measures from the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , as officials say they needed to tame market speculation threatening a fragile economic recovery.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par JAPAN FINANCE MINISTER NODA: WILL KEEP WATCHING YEN CAREFULLY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 TOKYO (Dow Jones)--Japan's finance minister said Thursday the government isn't aiming to push down the yen to any particular level, but vowed he will "continue to closely watch" the market--a sign he stands ready to order further \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 -market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  if necessary.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par BOJ EXPANDS ASSET-BUYING AND LOANS IN FACE OF STRONG YEN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Bank of Japan decided to expand its special fund for asset purchases and low-cost loans by a total of Y10 trillion Thursday to mitigate the negative impact of the strong yen on the economy. (published 2347 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par JAPAN ECONOMY MINISTER: JAPAN'S \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  ACTION SHOULD HAVE IMPACT ON SPECULATION NEAR TERM \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's economy minister said Thursday that the Japanese government's demonstration of its willingness to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market to prevent excessive moves in the yen will affect how speculators behave in the market in the near term. (published 0108 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par CHINA \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  REGULATOR: FACE RELATIVELY BIG NET \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  INFLOWS PRESSURES IN 2H \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China still faces "relative large" pressures from net \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  inflows, and will aggressively fight against the inflow of speculative cross-border funds, the country's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  regulator said Thursday. (published 0147 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par BANK OF JAPAN SUSPECTED OF BUYING DOLLARS VERSUS YEN ON EBS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is suspected of having continued its overnight market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  during London hours on Thursday, traders said, buying the dollar against the Japanese yen directly on \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  trading system EBS. (published 0105 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par UK OBR CHIEF CASTS DOUBT ON GROWTH FORECAST - REPORT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 LONDON (Dow Jones)--The head of the U.K. government's official forecaster, the Office for Budget Responsibility, Thursday cast doubt on the body's own growth forecast for 2011 in an interview with the Independent newspaper.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par INDIA FINANCE MINISTER: AIMING FOR HIGH GROWTH WITH MODERATE INFLATION \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 NEW DELHI (Dow Jones)--India's federal government aims to achieve high economic growth with moderate inflation, Finance Minister Pranab Mukherjee said Thursday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par DUTCH JULY INFLATION RISES, ABOVE EURO-ZONE AVERAGE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 AMSTERDAM (Dow Jones)--Dutch annual inflation was 2.6% in July, up from 2.3% a month earlier, and above the euro-zone average for the first time in more than 18 months, the Dutch statistics agency CBS said Thursday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par IMPROVING NEW ZEALAND 2Q EMPLOYMENT DATA ADD TO SUPPORT FOR ECONOMY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 New Zealand's unemployment rate was steady in the second quarter, providing some support for the economic recovery despite a devastating earthquake that struck the nation's second largest city of Christchurch in February. (published 2323 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par CHINA PENSION FUND TO INVEST CNY8 BLN IN CORPORATE BONDS - REPORT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's national pension fund plans to invest CNY8 billion in domestic corporate bonds and targets a cumulative yield of 30% over five years, state-run Shanghai Securities News reported Thursday. (published 0359 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par ECB EXPECTED TO SIGNAL GOVT BOND BUYING INTENTION - REPORT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is expected to signal it is stepping into the euro zone debt crisis on Thursday by reopening its purchases of government debt, amid fears the turmoil will claim the economy of a nation that is "too big to bail," the U.K.'s Daily Telegraph reported Thursday. (published 0053 GMT)\\\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 [ 04-08-11 0948GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1030 1804 4180   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020110804e784000z1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
