\par\par \b \uc2 Dow Jones Asia-Pacific Top Stories Sked For August 4\b0\par\par\uc2 2,301 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 August 2011\par 09:15\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 Following are the top Asia-Pacific stories featured on Dow Jones Newswires as of 0700 GMT. Not all stories appear on all wires. Please direct any questions or comments to asianewseds@dowjones.com.\par \par \uc2 MACRO/\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2 /FIXED INCOME:\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: BOJ EXPANDS ASSET-BUYING AND LOANS IN FACE OF STRONG YEN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Bank of Japan decided to expand its special fund for asset purchases and low-cost loans by a total of Y10 trillion Thursday to mitigate the negative impact of the strong yen on the economy. (published 0647 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par WSJ: \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 JAPAN\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  MOVES TO WEAKEN THE YEN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Japanese government \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Thursday morning in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets to stem the rise of the yen against the dollar, hoping to preserve modest growth in an economy rebounding surprisingly well from the March earthquake and tsunami--but that now appears threatened by a soaring \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  undermining exporters. (published 0153 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: IMPROVING NEW ZEALAND 2Q EMPLOYMENT DATA ADD TO SUPPORT FOR ECONOMY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 New Zealand's unemployment rate was steady in the second quarter, providing some support for the economic recovery despite a devastating earthquake that struck the nation's second largest city of Christchurch in February. (published 2323 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par S KOREA FIN MIN: MONITORING FOREIGN INVESTMENT IN DOMESTIC BONDS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korean Finance Minister Bahk Jae-wan Thursday said the government is closely monitoring foreign inflows into the domestic bond market and is considering various measures including greater regulation of the market. (published 0633 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par S KOREA FLAGS EXTERNAL RISKS, PLEDGES TO CONTAIN INFLATION \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korea's Ministry of Strategy and Finance Thursday reiterated that it will closely monitor economic conditions and ensure price stability. (published 0100 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par INVESTOR JIM ROGERS DOWN ON US DEBT DEAL, UP ON A$ \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Commodities and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  investor Jim Rogers said Thursday that the debt ceiling agreement reached in the U.S. will come back to haunt that country's economy but optimistic about the prospects for Australian and its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . (published 0024 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par INTERVIEW: HIGH KIWI A HEADWIND FOR ECONOMIC RECOVERY - NZ FINANCE MINISTER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The high New Zealand dollar is a headwind for the economy, New Zealand Finance Minister Bill English reiterated Thursday, but said there was little the government could do to limit its gains. (published 0430 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par DATA SNAP: INDIA PRIMARY ARTICLES WPI DOWN 0.6% IN WEEK TO JULY 23 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The wholesale price index for primary articles in India fell 0.6% to 196.9 in the week ended July 23, compared with a provisional 198.0 in the previous week, according to data issued Thursday by the Ministry of Commerce and Industry. (published 0639 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par DATA SNAP: MALAYSIA JUNE EXPORTS +8.6% ON YEAR; +6.0% EXPECTED \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Malaysia's June exports grew 8.6% from a year earlier as a sharp increase in palm oil, petroleum and gas exports offset a decline in electronic shipments. (published 0348 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par SINGAPORE MINISTER: GLOBAL ECONOMIC ENVIRONMENT HAS BECOME DICHOTOMOUS, VOLATILE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The global economic environment has become dichotomous and volatile with many developed countries still on a slow road to recovery while Asia continues to log strong growth, S. Iswaran, Singapore's minister in the prime minister's office, said Thursday. (published 0254 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par THAI \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CENTRAL BANK\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  REITERATES NO PLAN TO USE EXCHANGE RATE TO CURB INFLATION \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of Thailand\f28 \uc2 \f2  reiterated Wednesday it didn't plan to use exchange rates as a tool to combat escalating price pressures. (published 0308 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par VIETNAM NEEDS $48.8 BLN FOR POWER PROJECTS IN 2011-2020 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Vietnam will need to invest $48.8 billion in its power industry between this year and 2020, the Ministry of Industry and Trade said Thursday. (published 0234 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par NEW FOCUS AUTO TECH TO SELL AROUND CNY200 MLN OFFSHORE YUAN BONDS - SOURCE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 New Focus Auto Tech Holdings Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . plans to raise around CNY200 million by selling offshore yuan-denominated bonds with maturities of two years, a person familiar with the situation said Thursday. (published 0336 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par PREVIEW: INDONESIA 2Q GDP LIKELY SLOWED SLIGHTLY AS PRIVATE CONSUMPTION EASED \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Indonesia's economic growth likely eased slightly in the second quarter because private consumption, particularly of cars and motorcycles, slowed following the natural disasters that hit Japan earlier this year. (published 0429 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par PREVIEW: TAIWAN JULY INFLATION SEEN MODERATE; EXPORTS LIKELY DOWN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Taiwan's inflation pressure likely remained moderate in July as food prices fell after rising sharply in June, while exports growth likely slowed due to softening demand for the island's electronics and petrochemical products. (published 0242 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 EQUITIES:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par 3RD UPDATE: HITACHI, MITSUBISHI HEAVY MULLING MERGING SEVERAL OPS - SOURCE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Hitachi Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . and \f28 \uc2 \f2 Mitsubishi Heavy Industries Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . have been considering merging several of their \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  related to social infrastructure such as electric power and railways, a person close to the matter said Thursday. (published 0428 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: JS GROUP UNIT TO BUY ITALY'S PERMASTEELISA FOR Y63B \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japanese housing equipment maker \f28 \uc2 \f2 JS Group Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Thursday it will buy Italian building material company \f28 \uc2 \f2 Permasteelisa S.p.A\f28 \uc2 \f2 . in a deal valued at around EUR573 million, or Y63 billion, as it attempts to accelerate the expansion of its global reach. (published 0547 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par GMR AIRPORTS CONSIDERING BIDDING FOR MADRID, BARCELONA AIRPORT DEVELOPMENT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The airports division of \f28 \uc2 \f2 GMR Infrastructure Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . is considering putting in bids to develop airports in the Spanish cities of Barcelona and Madrid, the division's chief financial officer, Sidharth Kapur, said Thursday. (published 0548 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par COLLINS FOODS IPO FALLS ON DEBUT; DOWN 2% EARLY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Collins Foods Ltd. fell on its stock market debut Thursday, after conducting Australia's largest initial public offering so far this year. (published 0320 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par 2ND UPDATE: SINGAPORE'S OCBC 2Q NET RISES 15%; MISSES EXPECTATIONS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Oversea-Chinese Banking Corp. Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 ., Singapore's second largest bank by assets, Thursday reported a smaller-than-expected net profit increase of 15% on continued growth in its loans business and fee income, offsetting persistent pressure on mortgage margins. (published 0424 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: CAPITALAND 2Q NET PROFIT RISES 17.4%; POSITIVE ON SINGAPORE, CHINA \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 CapitaLand Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Thursday its second-quarter net profit rose 17.4% from a year earlier, mainly due to higher development profits in Singapore, fair value gains, and the sale of a residential site in China. (published 0020 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 SK TELECOM\f28 \uc2 \f2  2Q NET PROFIT KRW465.4 BLN; UP 3.7% VS YEAR EARLIER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 SK Telecom Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Thursday its second-quarter net profit rose 3.7% from a year earlier, thanks to more smartphone subscribers and rising sales at the company's non-telecom businesses. (published 0224 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 TORAY INDUSTRIES\f28 \uc2 \f2  1Q GRP NET PFT Y17.77B VS Y8.65B PFT YR EARLIER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Toray Industries Inc\f28 \uc2 \f2 . Thursday reported solid on-year gains in sales and profits for the first quarter ended June 30, due to a recovery in demand that allowed the for price hikes in various areas including textile, film and carbon fiber. (published 0440 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: BANK OF EAST ASIA 1ST-HALF NET PROFIT UP 29% AT HK$2.71 BLN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Bank Of \f28 \uc2 \f2 East Asia Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 ., Hong Kong's fifth-largest lender by assets, said Thursday its first-half net profit rose 29% from a year earlier, boosted by higher interest and fee-based income thanks to strong loan growth. (published 0542 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par RIO TINTO SAYS US, EU DEBT PROBLEMS A RISK TO OUTLOOK \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Rio Tinto PLC\f28 \uc2 \f2 , the world's second-largest iron ore miner by volume, said Thursday it's worried by sovereign debt risk in the U.S. and Europe as it reported record first half earnings. (published 0638 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par LEIGHTON EXPECTS FY11 NET LOSS OF AROUND A$408M \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Project developer and engineering contractor \f28 \uc2 \f2 Leighton Holdings Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . Thursday trimmed after tax guidance for last fiscal year to a net loss of A$408 million from an April estimate of A$427 million and confirmed an expected big swing to a profit this fiscal year of between A$600 million and A$650 million. (published 0009 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: TOLL ROAD OPERATOR TRANSURBAN BOOSTS PROFIT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Transurban Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  on Thursday reported a near doubling of annual profit and forecast a higher dividend this year after a widening of its flagship toll road in Melbourne boosted traffic volumes. (published 0205 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par DUET LAUNCHES A$227M SHARE ISSUE TO LOWER DEBT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 DUET Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  on Thursday launched a A$277 million entitlement offer to pay down debt after buying and selling assets to simplify its structure. (published 0003 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par GREAT WALL MOTOR: CHINA SECURITIES REGULATOR OKS FIRM'S CHINA IPO PLAN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Chinese automaker \f28 \uc2 \f2 Great Wall Motor Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Wednesday the China Securities Regulatory Commission approved its planned initial public offering in Shanghai. (published 0006 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: PTT CHEMICAL 3Q OPERATING PROFIT LIKELY WEAKER ON QUARTER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 PTT Chemical PCL\f28 \uc2 \f2  said its operating profit for the third quarter is likely lower than the second quarter but higher than the same period last year. (published 0504 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par METRO PACIFIC 1H NET PROFIT PHP3.25 BLN, UP 5.9% ON YEAR \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Metro Pacific Investments Corp. said Thursday its net profit in the first half of the year reached PHP3.25 billion, a 5.9% improvement from PHP3.07 billion a year earlier. (published 0538 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: ASIAN SHARES MIXED; YEN TUMBLES, NIKKEI CLIMBS ON \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 Asian shares were mixed Thursday, with the yen tumbling against its rivals and buoying Tokyo stocks after Japanese authorities \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to weaken the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . (published 0524 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ENERGY/COMMODITIES:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par 2ND UPDATE: NEWCREST SHUTS DOWN INDONESIA GOLD OUTPUT AFTER CRASH \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Newcrest Mining Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . has shut down production of one of its biggest gold \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  after a helicopter carrying employees and contractors crashed in Indonesia on Wednesday, killing all 10 people on board. (published 0529 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: URANIUM MINER ERA EMBARKS ON RANGER MINE EXPANSION \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 [ 04-08-11 0715GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Uranium miner \f28 \uc2 \f2 Energy Resources of Australia Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . approved Thursday the exploration of an untapped deposit that could extend the life of one of the world's biggest uranium mines. (published 0246 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par END OF FISHING BAN IN SOUTH CHINA SEA TO BOOST 'TEAPOT' \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 OPERATIONS\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 The end of the 11-week ban on fishing in the South China Sea earlier this week is bad news for Chinese fish but good news for the country's independent oil refiners in the south, traders and analysts said. (published 0535 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par STATE OIL COMPANIES TO POST INR1.22 TLN SALES LOSSES THIS FY - INDIA OIL MINISTER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 India's state-run fuel retailers will suffer a revenue loss of INR1.22 trillion in the current financial year due to selling some refined oil products at government-mandated prices, Oil Minister Jaipal Reddy said in Parliament Thursday. (published 0640 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par INTERVIEW: FONTERRA COOPERATIVE GROUP WANTS FARM SECTOR EMISSIONS EXEMPTION \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 New Zealand dairy giant Fonterra Co-Operative Group Ltd. expects to reduce emissions by 30% by 2030, the company's management said, but wants to be exempt from New Zealand's emissions trading scheme due to its economic impact. (published 0459 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par VIETNAM NEEDS $48.8 BLN FOR POWER PROJECTS IN 2011-2020 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Vietnam will need to invest $48.8 billion in its power industry between this year and 2020, the Ministry of Industry and Trade said Thursday. (published 0234 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par SANTOS CEO PLEDGES TO KEEP COAL SEAM GAS DRILLING CLEAN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The head of one of Australia's biggest coal seam gas companies, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Santos Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 ., said Thursday that its production of the unconventional fuel won't contaminate water supplies used by farmers. (published 0646 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par QATAR'S TASWEEQ OFFERS OCTOBER-SEPTEMBER TERM CONDENSATES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Qatar International Petroleum Marketing Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 ., or \f28 \uc2 \f2 Tasweeq\f28 \uc2 \f2 , issued a tender to sell term supplies of deodorized field condensate and low-sulfur condensate for October 2011 to September 2012, according to a tender document seen by Dow Jones Newswires Thursday. (published 0223 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par AUSTRALIA'S CAZALY SELLS IRON ORE PROJECT TO ASIAN INVESTOR \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -Australia's \f28 \uc2 \f2 Cazaly Resources Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Thursday it has agreed to sell its Parker Range iron ore project in Western Australia state to an undisclosed South East Asian investment group for a sale price of up to A$180 million. (published 0222 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par GINDALBIE METALS INKS 15-YEAR RAIL ACCESS DEAL FOR KARARA PROJECT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Gindalbie Metals Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Thursday it has signed a 15-year agreement with \f28 \uc2 \f2 WestNet Rail\f28 \uc2 \f2  to move output from its proposed Karara Iron Ore project in Western Australia state via the rail network. (published 0410 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par NEWMONT UNIT BATU HIJAU MINE \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 OPERATIONS\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  STILL SUSPENDED -SPOKESMAN \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  remain suspended at PT \f28 \uc2 \f2 Newmont Nusa Tenggara\f28 \uc2 \f2 's Batu Hijau gold and copper mine on Sumbawa island in eastern Indonesia after unsuccessful job seekers blocked access to the mine to protest the company's recruitment process, spokesman Ruby Purnomo said by phone Thursday. (published 0052 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: THAILAND 2011-12 SUGAR CANE OUTPUT MAY FALL 3.5% -OFFICIAL \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Heavy rain in Thailand's main sugar cane growing regions is threatening output, which might be about 3.5% lower than the previous season's crop, an official with the Office of the Cane and Sugar Board said late Wednesday. (published 0424 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par HALTING RARE EARTH OUTPUT 'UNREALISTIC' -INDUSTRY ASSOCIATION \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Stopping production and processing of rare earths is "unrealistic", an official with an industry association said Thursday, responding to an appeal by a \f28 \uc2 \f2 China Minmetals Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . unit. (published 0630 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CHINA CNGOIC: EDIBLE-OIL MARKET CAN TOLERATE 5% PRICE HIKE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Chinese edible oil retail market can tolerate a 5% price increase, though it isn't clear if all major producers will raise prices by that extent, the state-backed China National Grain and Oils Information Center said Thursday. (published 0218 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par WA REGULATOR RECOMMENDS AQUILA IRON ORE PROJECT APPROVAL \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Aquila Resources Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . has received the conditional support of regulators in Western Australia state for its multi-billion dollar West Pilbara iron ore project, a key step in its proposal to create a major new export venture to supply the Chinese steel industry. (published 0126 GMT) [ 04-08-11 0715GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 62550   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020110804e784000np\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
