\par\par \b \uc2 NZ Dollar Down Late As  \highlight22\uc2 Japan \highlight\uc2  Authorities  \highlight22\uc2 Intervene \highlight\uc2  In Market\b0\par\par\uc2 356 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 August 2011\par 08:23\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par                           Late        Change \par  NZD/USD                 0.8528       -0.0094 \par  NZD/AUD                 0.7981       -0.0033 \par  NZD/JPY                 67.585       +0.98 \par  April 2013 Bond         3.255%       +1.5 bps \par  May 2021 Bond           4.735%       -1.5 bps \par  10-Year U.S. Spread     +211 bps     -4.0 bps \par  90-Day Bank Bill        2.91%        -6.0 bps \par  \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 WELLINGTON (Dow Jones)--The New Zealand dollar was trading sharply lower late Thursday, after Japanese authorities \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the foreign \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets, buoying both the euro and the U.S. dollar against a host of regional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dealers said Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought dollars around the Y78.35 level through both Japanese and foreign banks, injecting roughly Y500 billion into the market. The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  wasn't unexpected, but the timing took some by surprise as it came at the outset of a scheduled two-day policy meeting by the Bank of Japan.\par \par \uc2 Westpac\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader Imre Speizer said the New Zealand dollar initially treaded water on the news, but fell sharply after officials confirmed the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . However, the slide "may only have an impact until U.S. equity markets open tonight," Speizer added.\par \par \uc2 Domestic second-quarter employment data released earlier in the day had little impact on the market as it came in within expectations and didn't alter the view the Reserve Bank of New Zealand would hike rates shortly.\par \par \uc2 The market is now focused on U.S. non-farm payrolls data due Friday.\par \par \uc2 New Zealand government bond curve flattened, while the 90-day bank bill fell as market expectations of the steepness of the RBNZ rate cycle moderated due to concerns about the international economic recover, said a local bond trader.\par \par \uc2 The New Zealand government bond tender was particularly well bid with NZ$560 million offered for the NZ$100 million worth of April 2023 bonds on offer.\par \par \uc2 The trader said demand for longer maturity bonds was strong due to global uncertainties.\par \par \uc2 -By Lucy Craymer, Dow Jones Newswires; 64-4-471-5990; lucy.craymer@dowjones.com [ 04-08-11 0623GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1062 20711 4171   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020110804e784000hp\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
