\par\par \b \uc2 MARKET TALK:  \highlight22\uc2 Japan Intervention \highlight\uc2  May Just Be First Volley - CS\b0\par\par\uc2 220 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 August 2011\par 03:40\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 0140 GMT [Dow Jones] The Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 's JPY-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  Thursday may be the first in a series of \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  over the coming weeks to curb further rises in the unit, and may have come Thursday in part as the \uc2 Swiss National Bank\uc2 's move Wednesday to weaken its own \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  made it easier for Japan also to step in, says Koji Fukaya, director of fixed income and global \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  research at \uc2 Credit Suisse\uc2 . "This may be the start of a number of actions, depending on the yen moves in the weeks ahead," Fukaya says. The SNB's move Wednesday means Japan's own move "could be considered as a kind of coordinated action" in response to broad USD weakness, he says. As traders say the MOF has so far sold under Y500 billion, Fukaya says the total size ahead could rise as high as Y2 trillion, though the move Thursday should be enough to send USD/JPY above 79.00 later, where it should stabilize in coming sessions.\par \par \uc2  The pair is now at 78.32, from 77.10 earlier.(andrew.monahan@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in Singapore. 65 64154 140; MarketTalk@dowjones.com \par  \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 [ 04-08-11 0140GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1012 1037 1085 5011 55117 75112   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020110804e78400036\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
