\par\par \b \uc2 MARKET TALK: BOC Declines To Comment On  \highlight22\uc2 Japan Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 1,348 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 August 2011\par 16:41\par \uc2 Dow Jones News Service\par \uc2 DJ\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 10:41 (Dow Jones) The \uc2 Bank of Canada\uc2  on Thursday said it would not comment on whether Canada's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  supports the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 's yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2 . BOC officials said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is "in regular contact with its international counterparts" as part of its ongoing monitoring of the global financial situation. "However," the BOC added, "it remains our policy not to comment on the specifics of those discussions." (Nirmala.Menon@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 10:38 (Dow Jones) Brazil's \uc2 Petrobras\uc2  (PBR PETR4.BR) making efforts to open lines of communication with the market after announcing $224.7B, five-year investment plan, says \uc2 HSBC\uc2 . That's a positive move, given PBR down 20% this year on investor disappointment with refining investments, firm says. \uc2 HSBC\uc2  looks for further progress in pre-salt development, especially increases to resource estimates, and successful bids for refinery design and drilling rigs as catalysts for PBR shares. \uc2 HSBC\uc2  maintains PBR at overweight, price target at $51.00 and BRL37.00. Shares recently down 2.7% at BRL21.70 in Sao Paulo; off 4.2% at $31.06 in NY. (jeff.fick@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 10:37 (Dow Jones) Options volume in \uc2 Bank of America\uc2  (BAC) is unusually heavy early in today's session, with BAC the most trafficked equity option in the market. Trading is dominated by a cautious 2-part trade as BAC hit a fresh 2-year low earlier. An investor purchased 15,000 October $9 puts funded by the sale of 30,000 October $8 puts. The net cost of the bearish "ratio spread" was zero, according to whatstrading.com analyst Frederic Ruffy. "Effectively, the customer owns the $8-9 put spread for free, but has significant downside if skew steepens [puts get pricier relative to calls] or BAC shares get into the sub-$7 range." BAC down 3.1% at $9.24. (christopher.dieterich@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 10:34 (Dow Jones) US stocks are experiencing another volatile session as the S&P 500 briefly hits correction territory, falling 10% from its May intraday high. Meanwhile, "We are setting ourselves up for a repeat of last summer," says Christian Thwaites at Sentinel Investments. Stocks slumped the same time a year ago, before Bernanke hinted at QE2 at Jackson Hole, sparking a huge rally to end the year. "Investors are waiting for the magic hand of QE3," says Thwaites. "Unfortunately we won't get it" as the risk of deflation is much less now than a year ago. "The market will continue to wrestle with a poor economy and no likelihood of immediate stimulus." Dow industrials down 170 at 11727. (steven.russolillo@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 10:32 (Dow Jones) Goodbye, pullback, hello, correction. At S&P 500's intraday low of 1233.31, it was 10% below the May 2 intraday high of 1370.58. Rule of thumb on Wall Street is declines of up to 10% are pullbacks, 10% to up to 20% are corrections and 20% or more are bear markets. Correction from April 29 closing high of 1363.61 would be 1227.25. S&P 500 has bounced slightly, no down 21 at 1239. Meanwhile, at DJIA's intraday low of 11673.74, it was 9.3% below its May 2 high of 12876, and 8.9% below its April 29 closing high of 12811. DJIA down 165 at 11731. (tomi.kilgore@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 10:30 (Dow Jones) Downgrading Dendreon (DNDN) is "not warranted or useful," Roth Capital says despite the stock plunging 65% to $12.62 after the drug maker said sales of its Provenge prostate-cancer drug are growing slower than expected. "Dendreon has conceded that there has been a much larger learning curve for the first-ever cancer vaccine approved in the US than expected." Still, Roth calls today's plunge an overreaction as it cuts its price target to $30 from $55 and maintains a buy investment rating. (ian.thomson@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 10:26 (Dow Jones) Stock-market action looking pretty ugly in the first hour, with selling intensifying once again. Particularly distressing is that attempts to rally back are being met with more waves of selling, taking the major averages to fresh lows after brief bounces. Buying on the dips not the best strategy so far today. Materials, energy, industrials and consumer discretionary among the hardest hit sectors so far. Euro continues to weaken, recently at $1.412, USD index up 1.5%. Oil recently at $90.34/bbl, down $1.59. DJIA down 172; Nasdaq off 56 or 2.1%; S&P 500 falls 22 to 1238. (john.shipman@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 10:21 (Dow Jones) There won't be any growth in the commercial-paper market for the rest of this year, at minimum, says Deborah Cunningham, chief investment officer at Federated Investors. She notes economic growth is very slow and that the US debt deal will have setbacks. "Offsetting that is the fact that the negotiation package is done, but investors may still stay on the sidelines. The contraction in the market will not be a big problem for companies because their daily needs are smaller." (anusha.shrivastava@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 10:17 (Dow Jones) There is no evidence so far in NY session of BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  on behalf of the MOF, but market remains on high alert for further yen-selling by BOJ, as Japanese officials remain determined to weaken value of Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Price action would also suggest BOJ has not been active, with USD/JPY grinding down and recently quoted at 79.08. Jens Nordvig of Nomura thinks BOJ will come back in the Asia session (or before if USD/JPY trades much lower). (andrewj.johnson@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 10:13 (Dow Jones) Symmetry Medical's (SMA) shares tumbling, down 8.7% at $9.13 after earlier falling more than 20% to 52-week low, as 2Q revenue falls short of analysts' expectations and SMA lowers full-year guidance, citing trends in orthopedic and medical-device industries. SMA says beginning in late May it's experienced lower volume trends in ortho industry driven partly by cuts in consumer spending. "Although SMA has rarely been a perfect predictor for the ortho market as a whole, we expect investors to view the back-half ortho recovery as facing greater risks in light of these results," Piper Jaffray says. Still, firm remains overweight. (corrie.driebusch@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 10:05 (Dow Jones) Alpha Natural (ANR) falls 7.1% at $37.22 as the coal producer swings a 2Q loss on acquisition expenses stemming from June's takeover of \uc2 Massey Energy\uc2 . The drop pays off for bearish options investors who earlier this week snapped up August $40 puts. Tuesday, a buyer picked up 10,000 bearish contracts for $1.13 apiece, according to Pipeline Trading Systems; those contracts last traded at $2.68. More than doubling the investment, at least on paper, in two days generated a $1.5M profit. (christopher.dieterich@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 10:00 (Dow Jones) Though 30-year fixed mortgage rates hit a record average low the past week, according to \uc2 Freddie Mac\uc2 , don't expect home purchases to pick up notably. Rates have been near current levels for more than a year--the average was 4.49% a year ago versus 4.39% the past week. But homebuying hasn't exactly been picking up as a result, with the Mortgage Bankers Association's home-purchase index being little changed the past year as well, sitting at mid-1990s levels. So if record-low borrowing rates can't entice people to get off the fence even as prices remain weak, is the rate of homebuying the past several years the new normal? (kevin.kingsbury@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par To contact the Equities Market Talk Editors, \par John Shipman, 212 416-2181,john.shipman@dowjones.com \par Paul Vigna, 212 416-2184,paul.vigna@dowjones.com \par Visit the Market Talk website at \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.djnmarkettalk.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.djnmarkettalk.com}}}\par \par \uc2 \f2 [ 08-04-11 1041ET ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 4035   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJ00000020110804e784000jn\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw427\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal6405\pichgoal600
