\par\par \b \uc2 News Highlights: Top Equities Stories Of The Day\b0\par\par\uc2 694 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 August 2011\par 14:00\par \uc2 Dow Jones News Service\par \uc2 DJ\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par TOP STORIES \par  \par GM PROFIT JUMPS 92% ON STRONG GLOBAL SALES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Auto maker's 2Q earnings surge to $2.5 billion, or $1.54 a share, as revenue soars, bolstered by stronger global sales and an increase in production of high-margin pickup trucks and SUVs in North America. Analysts forecast $1.20 a share. Shares gain 2% premarket.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par ECB HOLDS KEY RATE AT 1.5% AS DEBT CRISIS SPREADS \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  left its benchmark interest rate unchanged at 1.5%, as expected, as a deepening debt crisis threatens stability in Italy and Spain and recent data point to weakening economic growth.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 KRAFT FOODS\f28 \uc2 \f2  TO SPLIT INTO 2 PUBLICLY TRADED COMPANIES \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Kraft Foods\f28 \uc2 \f2  intends to separate into two publicly traded companies by separating its North American grocery business from its global snacks \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , becoming the latest big corporation to announce plans to split. Shares up 3% premarket.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CIGNA PROFIT RISES 39% AMID LOWER COSTS \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Cigna's 2Q earnings are up at $408 million, or $1.50 a share, as the managed-care company reports strong membership growth and lower health-claims costs. Revenue increases 2.9% to $5.51 billion. Analysts forecasted earnings of $1.29 a share.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par US STOCK FUTURES LOWER AHEAD OF JOBS DATA \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Stock futures drop as nervous investors show no appetite for extending the previous session's modest gains while awaiting the latest figures on weekly jobless claims. Kraft shares jump 8% premarket after announcing plans to split the company in two.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par JAPAN ACTS TO WEAKEN YEN, BOJ EASES FURTHER \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's government launches a yen-selling campaign backed up by Y10 trillion in easing measures from the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , as officials say they need to tame market speculation threatening a fragile economic recovery.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par BOE KEEPS RATES ON HOLD AS OUTLOOK DARKENS \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Bank of England keeps its key interest rate at a record low for the 30th straight month against a backdrop of slackening growth in the U.K. and gloomier prospects for the global economy.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par LEAR NET UP 11% ON BROAD GROWTH \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Lear 2Q earnings are up at $177.5 million, or $1.65 a share, as the auto-parts supplier reports higher sales across all regions, led by North America and Asia. Net sales climb 21% to $3.68 billion.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par RIO TINTO POSTS RECORD 1H NET, RAISES BUYBACK \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Rio Tinto\f28 \uc2 \f2 's 1H earnings surge to $7.6 billion even as it warns of sovereign-debt risk in the U.S. and Europe. The world's second-largest iron ore miner also lifts its share buyback plan to $7 billion from $5 billion.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par LEHMAN SETTLES LIQUIDATOR CLAIMS OF $20B \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Lehman Brothers Holdings\f28 \uc2 \f2  strike a deal with liquidators of its Hong Kong affiliate to settle US$20 billion worth of intercompany claims, marking an key step forward in the failed investment bank's liquidation process.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par GEITHNER EXPECTED TO STAY FOR FULL  TERM \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Treasury Secretary Timothy Geithner is expected to remain in his post for the remainder of President Barack Obama's term, the New York Times reports, citing officials familiar with discussions between Geithner and the White House.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par  \par  \par   ======= DOW JONES NEWSWIRES ANALYSIS AND COMMENTARIES ======= \par  \par MORNING BRIEFING \par Stock Futures Down As Jobs Data Loom \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Stocks are expected to open lower, as investors adopt a cautious stance ahead of key labor market data over the next two trading sessions. A string of downbeat economic readings out of the U.S. this week has depicts a weakening recovery for the world's largest economy.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par THE WALL STREET JOURNAL \par Yen \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Addresses Just One Of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's Many Woes \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Japanese government's decision to sell yen on global \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets came as a welcome respite for the country's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 -sensitive manufacturing sector. But the economic impact of that shot across the bow may be limited.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par   ============ U.S. MARKETS ACTION =========== \par DJIA              11896.44 from Wednesday \par NASDAQ             2693.07 from Wednesday \par S&P 500            1260.34 from Wednesday \par 10-year T-note    104 19/32 at 2.5880 yield \par NYMEX Crude       down $1.03 at $90.91/bbl \par Dollar/Euro       down 0.0094 at 1.4255 \par  \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 [ 08-04-11 0800ET ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 5030 55101   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJ00000020110804e78400080\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
