\par\par \b \uc2 Nikkei trims gains,  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 , BOJ easing impact limited\b0\par\par\uc2 746 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 August 2011\par 01:23\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Aozora, \uc2 Sony Financial\uc2 , Amada to become Nikkei 225 components\par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , monetary easing impact limited\par \par \uc2 * Hitachi and MHI climb, sources say in merger talks\par \par \uc2 * Longer-term gains seen hinging on U.S. jobs data\par \par \uc2 By Ayai Tomisawa\par \par \uc2 TOKYO, Aug 4 (Reuters) - The Nikkei average came off five-week lows on Thursday after \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to stem the yen's climb and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  eased monetary policy, but gave up earlier gains as worries about the global economy dominated.\par \par \uc2 Two of Japan's oldest conglomerates, industrial electronics maker \uc2 Hitachi Ltd\uc2  and heavy machinery maker \uc2 Mitsubishi Heavy Industries Ltd\uc2  , gained in heavy trade and supported market sentiment after sources said they may merge.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  pushed the yen down to about 79 yen to the dollar from a level of around 77 yen, but market players said that with the U.S. and euro zone economic and fiscal woes unresolved, the impact of Tokyo's solo \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  may be limited.\par \par \uc2 "The impact of the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  may be short-lived as the view that the yen is still a safe haven \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  hasn't changed amid concerns over the global economy," said Makoto Nagahori, head of equities at Instinet.\par \par \uc2 "If unemployment data confirms a stagnant recovery in the U.S. economy this Friday the dollar will likely fall, and the yen may rise again anyway," he said.\par \par \uc2 The benchmark Nikkei rose 0.2 percent to 9,659.18, while the broader Topix shed 0.1 percent to 826.36.\par \par \uc2 The Bank of Japan said its asset buying programme will be expanded to 15 trillion yen, an increase of 5 trillion. It also expanded a programme offering cheap fixed-rate funds via its market \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the same amount to 35 trillion yen and lifted its purchase target for exchanged traded funds to 1.4 trillion yen from 900 billion yen.\par \par \uc2 "The stock market is not very appreciative of today's easing and \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Ryoji Musha, president of Musha Research.\par \par \uc2 "First, it was not coordinated \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and also the yen's rise is due mainly to an investor shift to safe haven \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  amid concerns about the U.S. economy, not something that Japan can tackle on its own."\par \par \uc2 A merger of Hitachi and Mitsubishi Heavy would create one of the world's largest infrastructure firms with more than $150 billion in combined sales. Hitachi, the most actively traded firm by turnover on the main board, gained 1.7 percent to 471 yen and Mitsubishi Heavy rose 3.4 percent to 361 yen.\par \par \uc2 "It's going to be a history-changing event if true," said Fujio Ando, senior managing director at Chibagin Asset Management.\par \par \uc2 "It would really be praiseworthy if they can really move this forward because a merger would mean they would be creating a new company with companies from different ex-zaibatsu business groups. This used to be seen as extremely difficult."\par \par \uc2 The merger would be one of the largest ever in Japan. Hitachi, with a market value of $27 billion, would likely be the acquirer of Mitsubishi Heavy, valued at nearly $16 billion as of Wednesday's closing price. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^  \tab \par Starmine smartdata set on Hitachi/Mitsubishi Heavy:   \tab \par \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/jum92s"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/jum92s}}}\uc2 \f2   \tab \par ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^  \tab \par \tab \par  EXPORTERS GAIN ON \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 Exporters gained in heavy trade, with auto giant \f28 \uc2 \f2 Toyota Motor\f28 \uc2 \f2  rising 0.6 percent to 3,140 yen, and \f28 \uc2 \f2 Tokyo Electron\f28 \uc2 \f2  , the world's No.2 supplier of chipmaking equipment, adding 1.7 percent to 3,955 yen.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 However, Tokyo investors remained wary ahead of a crucial U.S. jobs report at the end of the week, which comes amid fears the American economy is stalling.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The pace of growth in the U.S. services sector fell in July to its lowest since February 2010 and the pace of U.S. private-sector job growth slowed in July with employers adding 114,000 positions, but the jobs additions exceeded \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par forecasts.  \tab \par   After the market close, the Nikkei publisher said that it\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 will add \f28 \uc2 \f2 Aozora Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2  , \f28 \uc2 \f2 Sony Financial\f28 \uc2 \f2  and Amada\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 to the Nikkei 225 benchmark.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 It said it would remove Mizuho Trust & Banking , Mizuho Securities and \f28 \uc2 \f2 CSK Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2  from the benchmark.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Volume was high, with about 2 billion shares changing hands on the Tokyo stock exchange's main board, the highest level since June 10. Declining shares slightly outnumbered advancing shares by 733 to 729.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (Additional reporting by Antoni Slodkowski; Editing by Michael Watson)\f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-JAPAN-STOCKS (UPDATE 