\par\par \b \uc2 REFILE-INTERVIEW-ADB subsidiary: monetary easing is best way to weaken yen\b0\par\par\uc2 By Kaori Kaneko   \par \uc2 279 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 August 2011\par 12:21\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Corrects spelling of 'institute' in paragraph 2)\par \par \uc2 TOKYO, Aug 3 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets would only have a temporary impact on the yen and bold monetary easing by the Bank of Japan would be more effective in stemming the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's strength, the head of an Asian Development Bank subsidiary said on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 Masahiro Kawai, dean and CEO of the Asian Development Bank Institute, which offers training to governments of ADB member nations, also said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  should send a strong message to the market that it is determined to beat deflation.\par \par \uc2 "I think monetary policy is the most important (way to stem the yen's rise)," Kawai, former deputy vice finance minister in charge of international affairs in Japan, told Reuters in an interview.\par \par \uc2 "What the Bank of Japan should do at the moment is take steps such as boldly expanding its asset buying programme or increasing its JGB purchases. There are various moves it could make."\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  kept markets on guard for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and BOJ easing on Wednesday as the finance minister vowed to stem the yen's ascent and the prime minister voiced concern over economic recovery.\par \par \uc2 Kawai said the prospect of further monetary easing by the Federal Reserve and concerns about the health of the U.S. economy would continue to weigh on the dollar, maintaining upward pressure on the yen.\par \par \uc2 "I don't deny that \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  would be effective at stemming the yen's rise temporarily. But it would be difficult to continue \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ."\par \par \uc2 (Editing by Joseph Radford)\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 JAPAN\b0 \highlight\uc2 -ECONOMY/ADB (URGENT, INTERVIEW) (CORRECTED)   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020110806e7830009b\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
