\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Yen falls as  \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervenes \highlight\uc2 ; euro slips on ECB\b0\par\par\uc2 647 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 August 2011\par 07:36\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold 1 trillion yen to weaken \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 * Analysts expect safe-haven yen, franc to remain strong\par \par \uc2 * ECB says would buy Portuguese, Irish bonds\par \par \uc2 (Updates prices, adds quotes, changes byline)\par \par \uc2 By Wanfeng Zhou\par \par \uc2 NEW YORK, Aug 4 (Reuters) - The yen fell sharply on Thursday after \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to curb its strength to support the country's export-led economy, but analysts did not expect any lasting impact given concerns about the global economy.\par \par \uc2 Official yen-selling pushed the dollar roughly 4 percent higher to 80.25 yen on trading platform EBS, well off a low of 76.29 set on Monday. On Wednesday, the \uc2 Swiss National Bank\uc2  had unexpectedly cut interest rates to cap a soaring Swiss franc.\par \par \uc2 The Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trimmed losses during New York trading, however, while the franc gained broadly as investors' strong demand for safe-haven assets persisted on fears a recovery in the global economy is losing momentum.\par \par \uc2 "The fact that our equity, bond and \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  indicators reveal a good number of real-money investors are seeking safety in respective asset markets and it's not just speculative activity driving the Swiss franc and yen higher suggests risk appetite is firmly on the back foot," said Samarjit Shankar, managing director of global \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategy at BNY Mellon in Boston.\par \par \uc2 The dollar last traded at 78.83 yen <JPY=>, up 2.3 percent on the day. The euro gained 1 percent to 111.43 yen <EURJPY=>.\par \par \uc2 Japan sold one trillion yen ($12.6 billion). Finance Minister Yoshihiko Noda said Japan had consulted its international partners but acted on its own. The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Asia and London pushed the yen to a three-week low against the dollar. For more see [ID:nL3E7J409F].\par \par \uc2 To support those efforts to weaken the yen, the Bank of Japan eased monetary policy by boosting asset purchases.\par \par \uc2 Japan's yen selling was its first since March 18 when the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  and other major central banks jointly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  after the yen surged to a record high versus the greenback.\par \par \uc2 Commerzbank\uc2  analyst Lutz Karpowitz said, however, that efforts by both Japan and Switzerland to weaken their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were unlikely to spark a trend reversal.\par \par \uc2 "There are hardly any alternatives for investors looking for a safe haven within the G10 universe," Karpowitz wrote in a note. "This fact is likely to prevent a stronger upward correction in dollar/yen. In the end we are therefore likely to see a sideways move."\par \par \uc2 <^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  tries to tame yen:               [ID:nL3E7J409F]\par  Timeline on yen \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 :          [ID:nL3E7J20DQ]\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  faces uphill battle on yen:      [ID:nL3E7J408Y]\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Past \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan FX intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 : \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/tyf82s"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/tyf82s}}}\par \par \uc2 \f2 ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^>\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The euro was last down 1.3 percent at $1.4137 <EUR=EBS>, having hit a two-week low of $1.4111 on EBS.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Traders noted more automatic sell orders under the $1.4100 area, with a break likely opening the way for a move lower to around $1.4068, the July 19 low.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  resumed buying government bonds after a four-month break and offered a new round of funding to commercial banks in response to a worsening euro zone debt crisis.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The ECB said after leaving interest rates unchanged at 1.5 percent that it would broaden its liquidity \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  as it revived its bond buying program in the secondary market by buying Portuguese and Irish bonds.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 But the Italian government bond yield premium over Bunds rose to euro era peaks as the ECB had no immediate plans for buying Italian and Spanish bonds. [ID:nL6E7J42I6]\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "The main takeaway from today's announcement is the limited prospects for further ECB tightening, which should weigh on the euro," said Vassili Serebriakov, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist at \f28 \uc2 \f2 Wells Fargo\f28 \uc2 \f2  in New York.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (Additional reporting by Julie Haviv; Editing by James Dalgleish)\f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 9)   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020110806e78300044\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
