\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Yen slides as Japan joins Swiss in fighting strong  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 577 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 August 2011\par 07:36\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  finmin confirms solo \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 * BOJ to end policy meeting Thursday, day ahead of schedule\par \par \uc2 * BOJ expected to ease monetary policy-source\par \par \uc2 * Margin traders cited as active cross/yen sellers\par \par \uc2 (Adds more comments)\par \par \uc2 By Chikafumi Hodo\par \par \uc2 TOKYO, Aug 4(Reuters) - The yen slid 2 percent versus the dollar on Thursday as \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to curb yen strength to support its export-led economy, one day after the Swiss \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  unveiled a shock cut in interest rates to cap a soaring Swiss franc.\par \par \uc2 Japanese Finance Minister Yoshihiko Noda confirmed that Tokyo had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, adding that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  by itself and that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  was communicating with other countries on the move.\par \par \uc2 Noda did not provide details, such as levels and the scale of the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market sources said the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  was \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market repeatedly to push down the yen. Recent gains in the yen have sparked fears that it could weigh on the country's economic recovery.\par \par \uc2 "The BOJ is \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  continuously, lifting the dollar versus the yen. We can see its willingness to keep the dollar above 78 yen," one \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market source in Tokyo said.\par \par \uc2 The Bank of Japan said it would end its monetary policy meeting on Thursday, a day ahead of schedule, and a source familiar with the BOJ's thinking said it is expected to ease monetary policy at the policy review.\par \par \uc2 The dollar surged 2.2 percent versus the yen to 78.81 yen\par \par \uc2 . The dollar had hit a four-month low of 76.29 yen earlier in the week, close to its record trough of 76.25 yen hit in March.\par \par \uc2 One resistance level for the dollar lies at 79.50 yen, a 61.8 percent retracement of the dollar's drop from an early July peak near 81.50 yen down to this week's four-month low.\par \par \uc2 "History suggests that the BOJ action will support USD/JPY for a few days at most but won't alter the overall trend. The Sept. 15, 2010 solo \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was very large scale but USD/JPY started to reverse within a matter of days," said Sean Callow, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist for Westpac Institutional Bank in Sydney.\par \par \uc2 Japanese retail investors and exporters were detected selling dollars against the yen after the dollar spiked up, dealers said. There was also talk of active selling of the Australian dollar against the yen by Japanese retail margin traders.\par \par \uc2 The yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  took place for the first time since March 18 when the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  and other central banks jointly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  after the yen surged to the record high versus the greenback after the quake.\par \par \uc2 The dollar has been under pressure against the yen after a series of weak U.S. indicators raised concerns about the U.S. economy's outlook.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Swiss National Bank\uc2  on Wednesday announced a shock cut in interest rates and threatened more action to cap a soaring Swiss franc. The SNB said it would cut its target rate to "as close to zero as possible" from an already rock-bottom 0.25 percent, and said it would very significantly increase the supply of francs to the money market over the next few days.\par \par \uc2 (Additional reporting by Masayuki Kitano and Reuters \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  analyst Rick Lloyd in Singapore; Editing by Kim Coghill)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 2)   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020110806e78300041\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw200\pich25\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3000\pichgoal375
