\par\par \b \uc2 News Highlights: Top Economic Stories Of The Day\b0\par\par\uc2 796 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 August 2011\par 12:58\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par WSJ: CHINA \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CENTRAL BANK\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  CHIEF WARNS ON US DEBT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 BEIJING (Dow Jones)--In his first public comments on Washington's debt deal, China's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  chief welcomed the passage of the bill that avoided a U.S. default but called on the U.S. to adopt "responsible measures" to manage its debt issues and pledged to continue diversifying China's dollar-dominated \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reserves.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par EURO-ZONE PRIVATE-SECTOR ACTIVITY SLOWS IN JULY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 LONDON (Dow Jones)--Activity in the euro zone's private sector grew at its slowest pace in 22 months in July, pulled down by contractions in Italy and Spain, a closely watched survey showed Wednesday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par SWISS FRANC PLUNGES AFTER SNB ACTS TO COUNTER STENGTH \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 LONDON (Dow Jones)--The Swiss franc fell rapidly against the euro and dollar Wednesday after the Swiss \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  surprised markets and introduced measures to tame the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's strength after its recent surge to record highs.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par PIMCO CHIEF: US DEBT PROBLEM TO SLOW GROWTH, WEAKEN DOLLAR-REPORT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The U.S. debt problem will result in slowing growth, rising unemployment and a weakening dollar, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Mohamed El-Erian\f28 \uc2 \f2 , chief executive and co-chief investment officer of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Pacific Investment Management Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 ., or Pimco, said in an interview published Wednesday. (published 0306 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par CHINA YUAN HITS ANOTHER HIGH LATE ON DOLLAR'S WEAKNESS OVERSEAS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's yuan rose against the U.S. dollar late Wednesday, hitting an intraday record high, tracking the euro's gains against the U.S. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the afternoon because of the Swiss \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's surprise announcement of measures to halt the Swiss franc's gains. (published 0226 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par GERMAN SURGE DRIVES EURO-ZONE JUNE RETAIL SALES PICKUP \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Retail sales in the 17 countries that share the euro rose at the fastest rate in over a year in June, although that surprisingly strong outcome was almost entirely due to a surge in German sales. (published 0240 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par ITALY APPROVES EUR7.3 BILLION IN FUNDING FOR INFRASTRUCTURE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 An Italian interministerial committee on Wednesday approved EUR7.3 billion in funding for infrastructure projects, most of them in the country's poor southern regions. (published 0355 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par SNB Cuts Rate To Zero To Help Counter Franc Strength \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ZURICH (Dow Jones)--The Swiss \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Wednesday said it has taken measures to counter the strong Swiss franc, and has trimmed its key three-month Libor rate target to as close to zero as possible, from 0.25%.\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 JAPAN\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  FINANCE MINISTER CALLS 1995 \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  "USEFUL REFERENCE" \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 TOKYO (Dow Jones)--\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's finance minister on Wednesday called the nation's 1995 efforts to fight yen rises through various forms of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  a "useful reference," suggesting he considers \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  a policy option to counter the yen's current rise.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par BOJ SHIRAKAWA: PAYING PARTICULAR ATTENTION TO NEGATIVE IMPACT OF YEN RISES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Bank of Japan Gov. Masaaki Shirakawa on Wednesday stepped up his warning against recent steep rises in the yen, amid increasing expectations for the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to ease monetary conditions further at its two-day meeting starting Thursday. (published 0508 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par PBOC Officials: China Should Gradually Loosen Control Over Lending, Deposit Rates \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 BEIJING (Dow Jones)--The time is becoming increasingly ripe for China to liberalize its interest rate system, and the country should gradually loosen control over lending rates and deposit rates, a group of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  officials wrote in an essay.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par INDIA FINANCE MINISTRY: NEED TO CALIBRATE DEMAND MANAGEMENT MEASURES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 NEW DELHI (Dow Jones)--India's federal government needs to carefully calibrate demand management measures aimed at controlling inflation, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 ministry of finance\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par US HASN'T GIVEN \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 JAPAN\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  SUPPORT FOR POSSIBLE \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCY INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  - SOURCE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The U.S. hasn't given its backing to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  for possible \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets, a person familiar with the matter told Dow Jones Newswires on Tuesday. (published 2200 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par CHINA PBOC GOV. CALLS ON U.S. TO MANAGE DEBT ISSUES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  governor on Wednesday welcomed the passage of a bill to raise the U.S. debt ceiling, but also called on the U.S. to adopt "responsible measures" to manage its debt issues. (published 0228 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par CHINA FINANCE MINISTRY TO RAISE AROUND CNY20 BLN IN 3RD SOVEREIGN BOND ISSUE IN HK - SOURCES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Ministry of Finance\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  plans to announce later Wednesday a plan to raise around CNY20 billion in its third yuan-denominated sovereign bond issue in Hong Kong, people familiar with the situation said. (published 0337 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par MOODY'S AFFIRMS US RATING; SAYS STEPS STILL NECESSARY OVER LONG-TERM \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Moody's Investors Service affirmed the U.S. government's top-notch rating Tuesday, but the country still needs to take further steps to improve its fiscal position over the long term. (published 2330 GMT) [ 03-08-11 1058GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1030 1804 4180   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020110803e783000ze\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
