\par\par \b \uc2 News Highlights: Top Economic Stories Of The Day\b0\par\par\uc2 756 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 August 2011\par 10:02\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par SWISS FRANC PLUNGES AFTER SNB ACTS TO COUNTER STENGTH \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 LONDON (Dow Jones)--The Swiss franc fell rapidly against the euro and dollar Wednesday after the Swiss \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  surprised markets and introduced measures to tame the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's strength after its recent surge to record highs.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par SNB Cuts Rate To Zero To Help Counter Franc Strength \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ZURICH (Dow Jones)--The Swiss \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Wednesday said it has taken measures to counter the strong Swiss franc, and has trimmed its key three-month Libor rate target to as close to zero as possible, from 0.25%.\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 JAPAN\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  FINANCE MINISTER CALLS 1995 \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  "USEFUL REFERENCE" \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 TOKYO (Dow Jones)--\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's finance minister on Wednesday called the nation's 1995 efforts to fight yen rises through various forms of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  a "useful reference," suggesting he considers \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  a policy option to counter the yen's current rise.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par BOJ SHIRAKAWA: PAYING PARTICULAR ATTENTION TO NEGATIVE IMPACT OF YEN RISES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Bank of Japan Gov. Masaaki Shirakawa on Wednesday stepped up his warning against recent steep rises in the yen, amid increasing expectations for the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to ease monetary conditions further at its two-day meeting starting Thursday. (published 0508 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par PBOC Officials: China Should Gradually Loosen Control Over Lending, Deposit Rates \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 BEIJING (Dow Jones)--The time is becoming increasingly ripe for China to liberalize its interest rate system, and the country should gradually loosen control over lending rates and deposit rates, a group of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  officials wrote in an essay.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par US HASN'T GIVEN \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 JAPAN\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  SUPPORT FOR POSSIBLE \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCY INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  - SOURCE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The U.S. hasn't given its backing to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  for possible \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets, a person familiar with the matter told Dow Jones Newswires on Tuesday. (published 2200 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par CHINA PBOC GOV. CALLS ON U.S. TO MANAGE DEBT ISSUES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  governor on Wednesday welcomed the passage of a bill to raise the U.S. debt ceiling, but also called on the U.S. to adopt "responsible measures" to manage its debt issues. (published 0228 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par CHINA FINANCE MINISTRY TO RAISE AROUND CNY20 BLN IN 3RD SOVEREIGN BOND ISSUE IN HK - SOURCES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Ministry of Finance\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  plans to announce later Wednesday a plan to raise around CNY20 billion in its third yuan-denominated sovereign bond issue in Hong Kong, people familiar with the situation said. (published 0337 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par MOODY'S AFFIRMS US RATING; SAYS STEPS STILL NECESSARY OVER LONG-TERM \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Moody's Investors Service affirmed the U.S. government's top-notch rating Tuesday, but the country still needs to take further steps to improve its fiscal position over the long term. (published 2330 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par TURKEY JULY CPI UP 6.31% ON YEAR, UNDERSHOOTS FORECAST \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Flling food prices saw Turkey's consumer price index in July fall on the month and undershoot expectations on the year, a development likely to please Turkey's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  as it continues to pursue its unorthodox monetary policy.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par GLOOM IN AUSTRALIAN RETAIL SECTOR SPREADS IN JUNE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Gloom in Australia's retail sector deepened in June with sales falling unexpectedly, with the outcome further eroding support for the Australian dollar, which touched its lowest levels since mid-July. (published 0231 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par HK MANUFACTURING ACTIVITY IMPROVES IN JULY, BUCKS ASIA TREND \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Hong Kong's manufacturing activity increased in July due to resumed growth in new orders, indicating an overall improvement in business conditions in the city, \f28 \uc2 \f2 HSBC Holdings PLC\f28 \uc2 \f2  said Wednesday. (published 0420 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par CHINA PBOC ADVISER: YUAN MAY NOT FLOAT IN NEXT 8-9 YEARS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The yuan may not float freely in the next eight to nine years because China faces economic reforms and global economic uncertainties, and China may instead continue to manage the yuan's exchange rate based on a basket of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , People's Bank of China adviser Xia Bin said in an essay in the latest issue of China Finance magazine. (published 0530 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par BLACKROCK EXECUTIVE: US DOWNGRADE WOULD AFFECT WIDE RANGE OF DEBT SECURITIES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A U.S. sovereign credit rating downgrade would have a huge impact beyond just Treasury prices, BlackRock Deputy Chief Investment Officer of Fixed Income Scott Thiel said Wednesday. (published 0339 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par BLACKROCK: SOVEREIGN WEALTH FUNDS HAVEN'T LOST FAITH IN EURO \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Sovereign wealth funds and other big-money investors haven't lost faith in the euro and aren't showing signs of a dramatic move away from euro assets, a senior money manager at \f28 \uc2 \f2 BlackRock Inc\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Wednesday. (published 0443 GMT) [ 03-08-11 0802GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1030 1804 4180   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020110803e783000pr\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
