\par\par \b \uc2 News Highlights: Top Economic Stories Of The Day\b0\par\par\uc2 790 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 August 2011\par 08:00\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par BOJ SHIRAKAWA: PAYING PARTICULAR ATTENTION TO NEGATIVE IMPACT OF YEN RISES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Bank of Japan Gov. Masaaki Shirakawa on Wednesday stepped up his warning against recent steep rises in the yen, amid increasing expectations for the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to ease monetary conditions further at its two-day meeting starting Thursday. (published 0508 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par UPDATE: US HASN'T GIVEN \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 JAPAN\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  SUPPORT FOR POSSIBLE \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCY INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  - SOURCE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The U.S. hasn't given its backing to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  for possible \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets, a person familiar with the matter told Dow Jones Newswires on Tuesday. (published 2200 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par UPDATE: CHINA PBOC GOV. CALLS ON U.S. TO MANAGE DEBT ISSUES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  governor on Wednesday welcomed the passage of a bill to raise the U.S. debt ceiling, but also called on the U.S. to adopt "responsible measures" to manage its debt issues. (published 0228 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par CHINA FINANCE MINISTRY TO RAISE AROUND CNY20 BLN IN 3RD SOVEREIGN BOND ISSUE IN HK - SOURCES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Ministry of Finance\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  plans to announce later Wednesday a plan to raise around CNY20 billion in its third yuan-denominated sovereign bond issue in Hong Kong, people familiar with the situation said. (published 0337 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par MOODY'S AFFIRMS US RATING; SAYS STEPS STILL NECESSARY OVER LONG-TERM \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Moody's Investors Service affirmed the U.S. government's top-notch rating Tuesday, but the country still needs to take further steps to improve its fiscal position over the long term. (published 2330 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par UPDATE: GLOOM IN AUSTRALIAN RETAIL SECTOR SPREADS IN JUNE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Gloom in Australia's retail sector deepened in June with sales falling unexpectedly, with the outcome further eroding support for the Australian dollar, which touched its lowest levels since mid-July. (published 0231 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par UPDATE: HK MANUFACTURING ACTIVITY IMPROVES IN JULY, BUCKS ASIA TREND \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Hong Kong's manufacturing activity increased in July due to resumed growth in new orders, indicating an overall improvement in business conditions in the city, \f28 \uc2 \f2 HSBC Holdings PLC\f28 \uc2 \f2  said Wednesday. (published 0420 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par UPDATE: CHINA PBOC ADVISER: YUAN MAY NOT FLOAT IN NEXT 8-9 YEARS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The yuan may not float freely in the next eight to nine years because China faces economic reforms and global economic uncertainties, and China may instead continue to manage the yuan's exchange rate based on a basket of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , People's Bank of China adviser Xia Bin said in an essay in the latest issue of China Finance magazine. (published 0530 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par BLACKROCK EXECUTIVE: US DOWNGRADE WOULD AFFECT WIDE RANGE OF DEBT SECURITIES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A U.S. sovereign credit rating downgrade would have a huge impact beyond just Treasury prices, BlackRock Deputy Chief Investment Officer of Fixed Income Scott Thiel said Wednesday. (published 0339 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par BLACKROCK: SOVEREIGN WEALTH FUNDS HAVEN'T LOST FAITH IN EURO \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Sovereign wealth funds and other big-money investors haven't lost faith in the euro and aren't showing signs of a dramatic move away from euro assets, a senior money manager at \f28 \uc2 \f2 BlackRock Inc\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Wednesday. (published 0443 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par CHINA'S LOCAL GOVERNMENTS HAMPER BEIJING BID TO CONTROL PRICES - RESEARCHERS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China is focusing on controlling inflation but heavy spending by local governments is hampering its efforts, commentaries in the official People's Daily said Wednesday. (published 0216 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par UPDATE: S&P ANALYST: PAKISTAN RATE CUT HAS NO RATING IMPLICATION \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \uc2 \f2 State Bank of Pakistan\f28 \uc2 \f2 's surprise 50 basis-point rate cut last weekend has no rating implication but reflects weak aggregate demand and low investments in the South Asian nation, a \f28 \uc2 \f2 Standard & Poor's\f28 \uc2 \f2  analyst said Wednesday. (published 0555 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par FOREIGN HOLDINGS OF INDONESIAN SECURITIES UP 43% ON YEAR IN JULY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Foreign holdings of Indonesian securities rose 43% in July to IDR1,391 trillion, from IDR971.039 trillion a year earlier, according to data from securities depository and settlement institution PT Kustodian Sentral Efek Indonesia. (published 0501 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par WORLD BANK UNIT PRICES 5-YEAR NZ$300 MILLION KAURI BOND - LEAD MANAGER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The International Bank for Reconstruction and Development, part of the World Bank Group, has priced a NZ$300 million, five-year bond, joint-lead manager \f28 \uc2 \f2 TD Securities\f28 \uc2 \f2  said Wednesday. (published 0459 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par INDONESIA TO OFFER 3-YEAR RETAIL BONDS ON OCTOBER 7-21 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Indonesia plans to offer three-year retail bonds, locally known as ORI, from Oct. 7 through Oct. 21, the finance ministry said Wednesday. (published 0516 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par    ======== DOW JONES NEWSWIRES ANALYSIS AND COMMENTARY ======== \par  \par  \par PREVIEW: PHILIPINES JULY INFLATION LIKELY 4.9%, HIGHEST IN OVER 2 YEARS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Inflation in the Philippines likely surged to its highest level in over two years in July, due to high food prices amid inclement weather conditions, while global oil prices remained elevated. (published 0341 GMT) [ 03-08-11 0600GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1030 1804 4180   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020110803e783000dz\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
