\par\par \b \uc2 News Highlights: Top Economic Stories Of The Day\b0\par\par\uc2 773 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 August 2011\par 07:00\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: US HASN'T GIVEN \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 JAPAN\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  SUPPORT FOR POSSIBLE \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCY INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  - SOURCE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The U.S. hasn't given its backing to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  for possible \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets, a person familiar with the matter told Dow Jones Newswires on Tuesday. (published 2200 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par CHINA FINANCE MINISTRY TO RAISE AROUND CNY20 BLN IN 3RD SOVEREIGN BOND ISSUE IN HK - SOURCES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Ministry of Finance\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  plans to announce later Wednesday a plan to raise around CNY20 billion in its third yuan-denominated sovereign bond issue in Hong Kong, people familiar with the situation said. (published 0337 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par MOODY'S AFFIRMS US RATING; SAYS STEPS STILL NECESSARY OVER LONG-TERM \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Moody's Investors Service affirmed the U.S. government's top-notch rating Tuesday, but the country still needs to take further steps to improve its fiscal position over the long term. (published 2330 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par UPDATE: CHINA PBOC GOV. CALLS ON U.S. TO MANAGE DEBT ISSUES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  governor on Wednesday welcomed the passage of a bill to raise the U.S. debt ceiling, but also called on the U.S. to adopt "responsible measures" to manage its debt issues. (published 0228 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par BLACKROCK EXECUTIVE: US DOWNGRADE WOULD AFFECT WIDE RANGE OF DEBT SECURITIES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A U.S. sovereign credit rating downgrade would have a huge impact beyond just Treasury prices, BlackRock Deputy Chief Investment Officer of Fixed Income Scott Thiel said Wednesday. (published 0339 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par CHINA'S LOCAL GOVERNMENTS HAMPER BEIJING BID TO CONTROL PRICES - RESEARCHERS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China is focusing on controlling inflation but heavy spending by local governments is hampering its efforts, commentaries in the official People's Daily said Wednesday. (published 0216 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par CHINA'S RAILWAY MINISTRY DEBT TOTALED CNY2.09 TRILLION AS AT END JUNE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The obligations of China's Railway Ministry rose to CNY2.09 trillion at the end of the first half from CNY1.98 trillion at the end of the first quarter, and its asset-liability ratio has reached 58.54%, according to a financial report posted by the Shanghai Clearing House on its website Monday. (published 0249 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par CHINA PBOC ADVISER: YUAN MAY NOT FLOAT FREELY IN NEXT 8-9 YEARS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The yuan may not float freely in the next eight to nine years because China faces economic reforms and global economic uncertainties, and China may instead continue to manage the yuan's exchange rate based on a basket of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , People's Bank of China adviser Xia Bin said in an essay in the latest issue of China Finance magazine. (published 0444 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par UPDATE: GLOOM IN AUSTRALIAN RETAIL SECTOR SPREADS IN JUNE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Gloom in Australia's retail sector deepened in June with sales falling unexpectedly, with the outcome further eroding support for the Australian dollar, which touched its lowest levels since mid-July. (published 0231 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par UK'S NIESR CUTS GDP FORECAST, URGES OSBORNE TO CUT TAXES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Chancellor of the Exchequer George Osborne should relax his tough austerity regime to boost sagging demand in the U.K. and not rely on the Bank of England to rescue the economy with more quantitative easing, a leading U.K. research group said Wednesday. (published 2301 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par UK SHOP PRICE INFLATION DIPS IN JULY AS FOOD PRICE RISES SLOW \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Shop price inflation in the U.K. slowed in July, aided by a slowdown in price rises for food, retailers said Wednesday. (published 2301 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 HSBC\f28 \uc2 \f2  HONG KONG JULY PMI 51.4 VS JUNE 50.3 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \uc2 \f2 HSBC\f28 \uc2 \f2  Hong Kong Purchasing Managers Index rose to 51.4 in July from 50.3 in June, boosted by an increase in new orders, \f28 \uc2 \f2 HSBC Holdings PLC\f28 \uc2 \f2  said Wednesday. (published 0235 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par UPDATE: WORLD BANK UNIT TO LAUNCH 5-YEAR NZ DOLLAR BOND -LEAD MANAGER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The International Bank for Reconstruction and Development, part of the World Bank Group, is set to launch a new five-year, New Zealand dollar-denominated bond, joint-lead manager ANZ said Wednesday. (published 0201 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par    ======== DOW JONES NEWSWIRES ANALYSIS AND COMMENTARY ======== \par  \par  \par PREVIEW: PHILIPINES JULY INFLATION LIKELY 4.9%, HIGHEST IN OVER 2 YEARS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Inflation in the Philippines likely surged to its highest level in over two years in July, due to high food prices amid inclement weather conditions, while global oil prices remained elevated. (published 0341 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par EURO-ZONE WORRIES STILL BOG DOWN COMMERCIAL PAPER MARKET \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Investors are back to worrying about euro-zone exposure now that the U.S. debt-ceiling impasse has been resolved. A good part of that concern is focused on the commercial paper market, a key source of short-term funding for foreign banks. (published 2015 GMT) [ 03-08-11 0500GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1030 1804 4180   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020110803e783000ab\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
