\par\par \b \uc2 Aussie, NZ dollars pause ahead of RBA rate decision\b0\par\par\uc2 526 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 August 2011\par 04:20\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 SYDNEY/WELLINGTON, Aug 2 (Reuters) - The New Zealand and Australian dollars sat below recent highs on Tuesday as investors grew cautious ahead of a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate statement, concerns about the global economy and possible yen \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 * The Aussie marks time at $1.0978, from $1.0969 in New York, ahead of the \uc2 Reserve Bank of Australia\uc2  (RBA) rate decision. It hit a 29-year peak of $1.1081 last week.\par \par \uc2 * The unceasing global uncertainty could argue against a hike in interest rates from the RBA, which holds its monthly policy meeting Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 * An announcement is due at 0430 GMT and most analysts assume it will keep rates at 4.75 pct , though there has to be some chance it will hike given core inflation has surprised on the upside for two quarters running.\par \par \uc2 * Markets imply only a 14 pct risk of a 25 basis point tightening.\par \par \uc2 * Domestic data added to the case against a move. Building approvals contracted 3.5 pct in June vs the median forecast for a 2.0 increase, while prices for houses slightly fell by 0.1 pct vs a 1.0 expected decline.\par \par \uc2 * Strong support for the Aussie seen from $1.0910, while resistance is at $1.1065 ahead of the high of $1.1081.\par \par \uc2 * Minor Fibo resistance at $1.1010, the 61.8 pct of Monday's $1.1066-$1.0923 and a break of that level would target congestion between $1.1030/70, according to a trader.\par \par \uc2 * Antipodeans resilient to global uncertainty as Asian stocks tumble on concerns the last minute U.S. deal will not be enough to prevent a U.S. rating downgrade.\par \par \uc2 * Sluggish global manufacturing data and talk of a possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken the yen added to market jitters.\par \par \uc2 * The New Zealand dollar sits lower at around $0.8745, from $0.8770 in New York. It looks to be consolidating after its recent heady run to a 30-year high of $0.8842 touched on Monday.\par \par \uc2 * Support at $0.8733, its daily low of Aug 1, and below that $0.8707. The latest high seen as the first line of resistance, after that $0.8856.\par \par \uc2 * The kiwi gives back some of its strong gains against the Aussie to trade around NZ$1.2533 after falling to a one-year low of NZ$1.2461 on Monday.\par \par \uc2 * New Zealand Q2 wages data rose 0.5 pct as expected for the quarter and 2.1 percent from a year ago, while employment numbers suggest the jobs market is slowly improving. None of the numbers seen posing any immediate inflation threat. See\par \par \uc2 * Full employment numbers on Thursday with expectations the jobless rate will stay static at 6.6 percent.\par \par \uc2 * NZ government bonds <0#NZTSY=> stronger sending yields 4 basis points lower along the curve. Interest rate futures <0#NBB:> modestly higher.\par \par \uc2 * Australian bond futures rallied amid the swing toward safety. The three-year contract <YTTc1> gained 0.09 points at 95.590, while the 10-year <YTCc1> rose 0.105 points to 95.205.\par \par \uc2 (Australia/New Zealand bureaux)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-AUSTRALIA-NEWZEALAND-\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2 /BONDS   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020110805e782000b0\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
