\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Japan \highlight\uc2  Edano:Refrain from comment on  \highlight22\uc2 forex intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 104 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 August 2011\par 03:09\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Aug 2 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's top government spokesman said on Tuesday he was refraining from making any comment on possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market.\par \par \uc2  Edano said he would be watching the dollar's weakness with strong interest.\par \par \uc2  He made the comments after the dollar fell to near its record low against the yen on Monday, which heightened the possibility of Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken the yen and for the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to follow suit with additional monetary easing.  \par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Kaori Kaneko; Editing by Michael Watson)\par \par \uc2 JAPAN-ECONOMY/EDANO (URGENT)   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020110805e782000al\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
