\par\par \b \uc2 WORLD  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 : Global Growth, Debt Fears Grip  \highlight22\uc2 Currency \highlight\uc2  Markets\b0\par\par\uc2 715 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 August 2011\par 13:20\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 --Global growth fears coupled with euro-zone worries grip \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets\par \par \uc2 --Swiss franc benefits, hitting record high against the euro\par \par \uc2 --Dollar mostly higher, Australian dollar pressured after dovish-sounding RBA\par \par \uc2 By Clare Connaghan\par \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES\par \par \uc2 LONDON (Dow Jones)--A toxic mix of global economic growth concerns and worries about the euro-zone sovereign debt crisis sent riskier \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  into a tailspin in European trading Tuesday, with the euro hitting a fresh-all-time low against the Swiss franc.\par \par \uc2 The dollar was mostly higher, while speculation \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  could conduct yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  left \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  investors running to the cover of the Swiss \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "With fear of Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  ever more elevated, the Swiss franc is again proving the primary conduit for risk sentiment," said \uc2 Adam Cole\uc2 , global head of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  at \uc2 RBC Capital Markets\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Japanese Finance Minister Yoshihiko Noda said he would "like to watch market movements closely today, particularly after the progress in the U.S. debt issue," adding that the government is talking with the Bank of Japan and other countries about yen strength.\par \par \uc2 The yen was stable against the dollar in Europe, trading at Y77.44 by 1109 GMT, compared with Y77.18 late Monday in New York.\par \par \uc2 Worries about the euro-zone sovereign debt crisis sent Italian and Spanish bonds yields to their widest levels since the inception of the common \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , while default insurance costs for Italy and Spain hit record highs.\par \par \uc2 "The market is still obviously nervous," said Daragh Maher, deputy head of global \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategy at \uc2 Credit Agricole\uc2  in London.\par \par \uc2 Adding to market concerns are weakening economic fundamentals following a spate of weak manufacturing readings in the U.S., China and the euro zone, as well as the nagging likelihood of a U.S. credit-rating downgrade, even as a last-minute deal to raise the U.S. debt ceiling passes through Congress.\par \par \uc2 "Markets continued to trade in a risk-off mode, despite the U.S. House of Representatives comfortably approving to raise the debt ceiling overnight," said \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist Chris Walker at UBS AG.\par \par \uc2 Adding to the negative tone was Australia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which failed to meet market expectations that it would signal an increasing likelihood of rate hikes down the road. The Australian dollar fell after the \uc2 Reserve Bank of Australia\uc2  signaled it may hold off from further tightening until volatility in global markets eases.\par \par \uc2 U.S. personal income and spending is due for release at 1230 GMT.\par \par \uc2 At 1106 GMT, the euro was trading at $1.4198 against the dollar, compared with $1.4250 late Monday in New York, according to trading system EBS. The euro was at Y109.850 compared with Y110.01. The pound was at $1.6277 against the dollar, compared with $1.6320 late Monday in New York.\par \par \uc2 The ICE Dollar Index, which tracks the dollar against a trade-weighted basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , was at 74.548 compared with 74.329 late Monday in New York.\par \par \uc2 A summary of key levels for chart-watching technical strategists is below:\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  spot:       EUR/USD    USD/JPY    GBP/USD    USD/CHF \par  \par Spot 1022 GMT     1.4202     77.30      1.6282     0.7795 \par 3 Day Trend       Bearish    Bearish    Bearish    Bearish \par Weekly Trend      Bullish    Bearish    Bullish    Bearish \par 200 day ma        1.4017     82.04      1.6075     0.9031 \par 3rd Resistance    1.4350     78.05      1.6420     0.8000 \par 2nd Resistance    1.4283     77.85      1.6364     0.7954 \par 1st Resistance    1.4258     77.72      1.6327     0.7857 \par Pivot*            1.4297     77.18      1.6339     0.7840 \par 1st Support       1.4157     77.16      1.6244     0.7758 \par 2nd Support       1.4138     77.00      1.6192     0.7732 \par 3rd Support       1.4014     76.65      1.6130     0.7675 \par  \par  \par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  spot:       EUR/GBP \par  \par Spot 1021 GMT     0.8723 \par 3 Day Trend       Bearish \par Weekly Trend      Bearish \par 200 day ma        0.8717 \par 3rd Resistance    0.8882 \par 2nd Resistance    0.8804 \par 1st Resistance    0.8753 \par Pivot*            0.8757 \par 1st Support       0.8693 \par 2nd Support       0.8611 \par 3rd Support       0.8510 \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Clare Connaghan, Dow Jones Newswires; +44 (0) 20 7842 9496, clare.connaghan@dowjones.com\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (Dow Jones Technical Strategist Francis Bray contributed to this article.) [ 02-08-11 1120GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1035 28038 4163 44462   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020110802e782000yg\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
