\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE: BOJ WATCH: Policy Board To Discuss Steps Against Strong Yen\b0\par\par\uc2 865 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 August 2011\par 10:04\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 (Adds table of results of survey of economists)\par \par \uc2 By Megumi Fujikawa\par \par \uc2 A Dow Jones Newswires Column\par \par \uc2 TOKYO (Dow Jones)--The Bank of Japan will likely discuss additional monetary easing steps to counter the negative impact of a strong yen on the economy when its policy board meets later this week, and such measures could come in tandem with the government's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market.\par \par \uc2 If the BOJ were to take action, the most likely option would be to increase its purchases of assets such as government and corporate debt, in a bid to lower long-term rates and also prevent a deterioration of market sentiment, people with knowledge of the bank's thinking said.\par \par \uc2 BOJ officials have become increasingly concerned that the higher yen will weigh on business and household sentiment, interfering with an economic recovery from the devastation of the March 11 earthquake and tsunami.\par \par \uc2 They are also concerned that the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's rise, coupled with the unstable power supply, may lead domestic firms to further shift their \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  overseas.\par \par \uc2 Referring to the yen's rise, BOJ Gov. Masaaki Shirakawa recently said: "It could have adverse effects on the economy as a whole through a decline in exports and corporate profits."\par \par \uc2 The two-day meeting of the policy board from Thursday has gained increased attention as government officials step up their warnings over the yen's appreciation, inviting expectations that the authorities may \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  soon to stem its rise.\par \par \uc2 "\b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  can conduct \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  at any time," a person familiar with \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy affairs told Dow Jones Newswires on Tuesday, although the source declined to say how close the authorities are to taking action.\par \par \uc2 The yen has been rising quickly in the past few days due to uncertainty over the U.S. debt ceiling issue. The dollar declined to Y76.29 on Monday, near an all-time low of Y76.25 hit on March 17.\par \par \uc2 Some Cabinet ministers have also called on the BOJ to do its share to tackle the strong yen, which eats away at the profits of Japan's exporters, its key engine of growth.\par \par \uc2 Japan's national strategy minister said Tuesday that monetary policy is among the policy responses needed if the yen continues to rise, the Nikkei reported.\par \par \uc2 "A response that includes monetary policy will become necessary," Koichiro Genba was quoted as saying.\par \par \uc2 The BOJ has been buying a variety of financial assets, from government and corporate bonds to exchange-traded funds and even real-estate investment trusts through a fund. Within days of the March disaster, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  doubled the size of the fund to Y10 trillion.\par \par \uc2 If the firmer yen and ensuing stock falls deepen the nation's long-lasting problem of deflation, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could further boost purchases of short-term government bills and commercial paper, said \uc2 Barclays Capital\uc2  chief Japan economist Kyohei Morita.\par \par \uc2 The bank could also decide to buy longer-maturity government debt, such as bonds with a maturity of five years, rather than the current one to two years, under the asset-buying program, he added.\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Survey results (in alphabetical order): \par  \par                             August 5 Action \par  \par \f28 \uc2 \f2 Barclays Capital\f28 \uc2 \f2             Unchanged \par (Kyohei Morita) \par  \par Dai-ichi Life Research      Unchanged \par (Hideo Kumano) \par  \par Daiwa Sec Capital Markets   Unchanged \par (Maiko Noguchi) \par  \par Mitsubishi UFJ              Up Asset Buying By Y5 Tln \par Morgan Stanley Securities \par (Naomi Hasegawa) \par  \par Mizuho Research             Unchanged \par (Yasuo Yamamoto)            Up Asset Buying By Y3-5 Tln, If USD Around Y75-Y76 \par  \par Mizuho Securities           Unchanged \par (Yasunari Ueno) \par  \par Norinchukin Research        Unchanged \par (Takeshi Minami) \par  \par RBS Securities              Up Asset Buying By Y5 Tln, Especially T-bills \par (Junko Nishioka) \par  \par SMBC Nikko Securities       Up Asset Buying By Y5 Tln \par (Mari Iwashita)             If Financial Markets Get Volatile \par  \par Totan Research              Up Asset Buying By Y5 Tln \par (Kiyoshi Iida) \par  \par  \par                             Next Action \par  \par \f28 \uc2 \f2 Barclays Capital\f28 \uc2 \f2             Up Buying Of CP, T-bills To Y4 Tln Each, JGBs To Y5 Tln, \par (Kyohei Morita)             Including JGBs With Maturity Of Up To 5 Years, \par                             Only If JPY Rises, Nikkei Falls To Near 9,000 \par  \par Dai-ichi Life Research      No Action For A While \par (Hideo Kumano) \par  \par Daiwa Sec Capital Markets   No Action For A While \par (Maiko Noguchi) \par  \par Mitsubishi UFJ              No Action For A While \par Morgan Stanley Securities \par (Naomi Hasegawa) \par  \par Mizuho Research             No Action For A While \par (Yasuo Yamamoto)            May Up Asset Buying If JPY Rises Further \par  \par Mizuho Securities           Up Asset Buying By Y5 Tln In Or After Autumn \par (Yasunari Ueno) \par  \par Norinchukin Research        Up Asset Buying By Y5 Tln In October \par (Takeshi Minami) \par  \par RBS Securities              Next Action Depends On JPY, Stock Moves \par (Junko Nishioka)            (Up Asset Buying If Necessary) \par  \par SMBC Nikko Securities       Up Asset Buying By Y5 Tln Around Autumn \par (Mari Iwashita) \par  \par Totan Research              No Forecast \par (Kiyoshi Iida) \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Megumi Fujikawa, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-6269-2786; megumi.fujikawa@dowjones.com\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 TALK BACK: We invite readers to send us comments on this or other financial news topics. Please email us at TalkbackAsia@dowjones.com. Readers should include their full names, work or home addresses and telephone numbers for verification purposes. We reserve the right to edit and publish your comments along with your name; we reserve the right not to publish reader comments. [ 02-08-11 0804GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1042 4131   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020110802e782000p0\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
