\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  ASIA: Market Ready For Imminent  \highlight22\uc2 Japan Intervention \highlight\uc2 , But Has Doubts Over Effects\b0\par\par\uc2 511 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 August 2011\par 09:36\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 -- Market believes \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  may be around the corner\par \par \uc2 -- Buying during New York trading hours seen as possible\par \par \uc2 -- BOJ's easing to maximize \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  effects an option\par \par \uc2 -- Market still skeptical over change of longer-term impact\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    By Takashi Mochizuki \par    Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 TOKYO (Dow Jones)--With Japanese officials being made increasingly uncomfortable by the strength of the yen, Tokyo traders now believe a yen-selling \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  may be just around the corner, even as they doubt that it will change market fundamentals.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan may weigh into the market this week, the dealers said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Some speculate that such a step could be coupled with further easing by the Bank of Japan in order to increase its impact. The BOJ's policy board is scheduled to meet Thursday and Friday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Finance Minister Yoshihiko Noda on Tuesday escalated his warnings about the yen, calling it "strongly overvalued." As of 0649 GMT, the greenback was around Y77.30 after touching Y76.29 on Monday, just few points away from the post-war low of Y76.25 marked on March 17.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Traders took the remark to suggest that authorities are now looking more closely at the absolute value of the yen after previously focusing on market volatility.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "Fast-paced gains in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  are no longer necessary to trigger Japanese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ," said Kenichiro Ikezawa, a senior fund manager at \f28 \uc2 \f2 Daiwa SB Investments\f28 \uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 While Ikezawa believes that \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is possible any time, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Barclays Capital\f28 \uc2 \f2  chief \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist Masafumi Yamamoto said the MOF may wait until Friday, when the U.S. releases market-moving non-farm payrolls data.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  before the U.S. jobs data may end up a failure if the report turns out to be disappointing and propels a fresh round of dollar-selling," Yamamoto said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 He said that it's possible for the MOF to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the market during New York trading, or after the release of the jobs data, if they fall short of market expectations and yen is rising.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Expectations are also rising that the BOJ will play a role in weakening the yen. \f28 \uc2 \f2 JP Morgan\f28 \uc2 \f2  said the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  may expand the size of its asset-buying program at its two-day meeting ending on Friday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Even if there is coordinated action, analysts say they are doubtful that the efforts would produce any fundamental changes in the market's dynamics.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Tohru Sasaki, chief strategist at \f28 \uc2 \f2 JP Morgan\f28 \uc2 \f2 , said "the dollar is unlikely to reach Y80," which is a key level for exporters In the recent past cases, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was started at Y79.18 on March 18, pushing the dollar up to Y82.00 and in September from Y83.00 to Y85.78, Sasaki said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Ikezawa also believes effects of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  won't last for more than two weeks as investors' key focus is on the U.S. economic fundamentals and European debt issues, neither of which look promising.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Takashi Mochizuki, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-6269-2782; takashi.mochizuki@dowjones.com [ 02-08-11 0736GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020110802e782000mh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
