\par\par \b \uc2 MARKET TALK: Asian Summary; Japan Raises Concerns About Strong JPY\b0\par\par\uc2 358 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 August 2011\par 08:00\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 0600 GMT [Dow Jones] ASIAN SUMMARY: Regional markets are lower as fresh worries over the global growth outlook offset relief over an 11th-hour deal to raise the U.S. debt ceiling. The Nikkei is down 1.2%, the S&P/ASX is off 1.3%, the HSI is 0.6% lower, the Kospi is down 2.2%, the Taiex is down 1.3%, the Sensex is down 1.0%, the Shanghai Composite is off 1.5%, the STI is down 1.1%, and the NZX-50 is down 0.5%. In \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets, speculation that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  could conduct JPY-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  sent the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  lower; Japanese Finance Minister Yoshihiko Noda said he would "like to watch market movements closely today, particularly after the progress in the U.S. debt issue," adding that the government is talking with the BOJ and other countries about the JPY's strength. The USD/JPY is at 77.38 from 77.18 late Monday in New York. The EUR/USD is at 1.4248 from 1.4250 and the EUR/JPY is at 110.26 from 110.01.\par \par \uc2  The AUD/USD fell after the RBA left its cash rate steady at 4.75% for a 10th month in succession; the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  lists global uncertainties high among its reasons for caution. The pair is at 1.0924 from 1.0977 before the decision. The total number of Australian houses and apartments approved for construction fell a seasonally adjusted 3.5% in June from May. The BOK said it increased the amount of gold held as part of the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves for the first time in 13 years. Korea's foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves rose to a record high of $311.03 billion at the end of July. Spot gold is at $1,623.80, up $3.50 from the NY close. September Nymex crude oil futures are down 24 cents at $94.65/bbl. (philip.vahn@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in Singapore. 65 64154 140; MarketTalk@dowjones.com \par  \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 [ 02-08-11 0600GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1012 1085 75112 75117   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020110802e782000cd\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
