BA ON-HOLD RATES VERDICT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Debt woes in the U.S. and Europe sealed a decision Tuesday by Australia's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to keep interest rates steady in August, and economists now say policy will be left unchanged until early 2012. (published 0540 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par MOODY'S CREDIT OFFICERS IN TOKYO FOR MEETINGS WITH JAPAN OFFICIALS-SOURCES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A delegation of credit rating officers from Moody's Investors Service is visiting Tokyo for talks with Japanese officials as it prepares to conclude a review on the country's sovereign debt rating for a possible downgrade, people familiar with the matter said Tuesday. (published 0303 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par US HOUSE VOTES 269-161 TO PASS DEBT CEILING INCREASE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 U.S. House members voted to increase the debt ceiling and cut $2.1 trillion from the budget deficit Monday evening, sending a historic blueprint for the nation's fiscal future on to the Senate as lawmakers sought to avert an economic disaster the day before the nation could begin defaulting on some obligations. (published 2318 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par BANK OF CHINA LAUNCHES YUAN CASH BUSINESS IN ZAMBIA; EYES WIDER AFRICAN ROLE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Bank of China Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 ., the country's fourth-largest lender by assets, said Tuesday it launched yuan cash business services in Zambia with the aim of boosting economic ties between China and Africa. (published 0147 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par XINHUA: WINDOW AROUND AUG 10 FOR POSSIBLE CHINA RATE HIKE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A key window for a possible rate increase in China is around Aug. 10 and the country's current rate hike cycle will likely be over if the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  doesn't move at that time, Xinhua news agency said. (published 0242 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \