\par\par \b \uc2 Dow Jones Asia-Pacific Top Stories Sked For August 2\b0\par\par\uc2 2,042 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 August 2011\par 09:12\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 Following are the top Asia-Pacific stories featured on Dow Jones Newswires as of 0700 GMT. Not all stories appear on all wires. Please direct any questions or comments to asianewseds@dowjones.com.\par \par \uc2 MACRO/\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2 /FIXED INCOME:\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par 2ND UPDATE: JAPAN'S FINANCE MINISTER UPS RHETORIC, CALLS YEN "STRONGLY OVERVALUED" \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's finance minister Tuesday called the yen "strongly overvalued" and made it clear he has been in touch with overseas authorities on \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  matters, fueling speculation the government may step in to stem the yen's steady rise. (published 0556 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par JAPAN FINANCE MINISTER: WON'T TALK ABOUT YEN RATE RANGE FOR \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's finance minister on Tuesday declined to comment on whether the yen is already in a range that could prompt Tokyo authorities to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market. (published 0619 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par MOODY'S CREDIT OFFICERS IN TOKYO FOR MEETINGS WITH JAPAN OFFICIALS-SOURCES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A delegation of credit rating officers from Moody's Investors Service is visiting Tokyo for talks with Japanese officials as it prepares to conclude a review on the country's sovereign debt rating for a possible downgrade, people familiar with the matter said Tuesday. (published 0303 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par 2ND UPDATE: US, EUROPE DEBT UPHEAVALS SEAL RBA ON-HOLD VERDICT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Debt crises in the U.S. and Europe sealed a decision Tuesday by Australia's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to keep interest rates steady in August, and economists now say policy will be left unchanged until early 2012. (published 0608 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: CHINA RESUMES PRESSURE ON U.S. TO RESOLVE DEBT PROBLEMS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China stepped up its public pressure on the U.S. Tuesday, calling for a resolution of long-term fiscal challenges even as the House passed a agreement to raise the country's debt ceiling to avert a potential government default. (published 0347 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CHINA STATE PLANNER SAYS MAINTAINING STABLE PRICES IS KEY GOAL \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China will continue to put maintaining price stability as its top priority in the second half of the year, a spokesman for China's top economic planner said Tuesday. (published 0658 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CHINA RESEARCHER: SHOULD EXPAND SCALE OF SOVEREIGN WEALTH FUNDS, INVEST IN INDUSTRY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China should expand the scale of its sovereign wealth funds and switch from financial investment to industrial investment to protect its massive \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reserves, a state researcher said Tuesday. (published 2341 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: STORMY AUSTRALIAN HOUSING OUTLOOK ADDS TO ECONOMIC WOES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australian building approvals remained in the doldrums in June, dispelling expectations of a rebound and signaling weak consumer confidence, as talk of rising interest rates continues to take a toll on industry confidence. (published 0234 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par AUSTRALIAN CORPORATES FACE US$548B OF DEBT REFINANCING THROUGH 2015 -S&P \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australia's corporate sector is facing some US$548 billion of debt refinancing through to the end of 2015, 99% of which is from investment grade-rated entities, according to analysis conducted by \f28 \uc2 \f2 Standard & Poor's\f28 \uc2 \f2 . (published 0001 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par THAI \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CENTRAL BANK\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 : MONETARY POLICY STILL NEEDS TO FOCUS ON INFLATION \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of Thailand\f28 \uc2 \f2 's monetary policy still needs to focus on controlling inflation, despite concerns that a higher interest rate would draw more inflows and drive further appreciation of the baht, the bank's Deputy Gov. Atchana Waiquamdee said Tuesday. (published 0644 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par INDONESIA ECONOMY CHIEF: CAUTIOUS ON INFLATION, 2011 EXPORTS MAY REACH UP TO $200B \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Indonesia's Coordinating Minister for Economy Hatta Rajasa said Tuesday that he remains cautious on inflation in August as price pressures tend to pick up during the Islamic fasting month that started Monday. (published 0547 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par INDIA GOVERNMENT SEEKS PARLIAMENT OK TO SPEND EXTRA INR90.16 BLN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Indian government Tuesday sought Parliament's approval to spend a further INR90.16 billion on a net basis, its first demand for additional expenditure for this fiscal year to March 31 over its initial budget estimate. (published 0651 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: NACF PRICES $500 MLN 5.5-YR DOLLAR BOND AT 99.569 TO YIELD 3.587% - SOURCES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korea's National Agricultural Cooperative Federation has priced a $500 million 5.5-year global dollar bond at 99.569 to yield 3.587%, two people familiar with the deal said Tuesday. (published 0332 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CHINA EASTERN AIR: PRICED 3-YEAR OFFSHORE YUAN BOND ISSUE AT PAR WITH 4% YIELD \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China Eastern Airlines Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Tuesday it priced its three-year offshore yuan bond at par with a yield of 4%, raising CNY2.50 billion. (published 2358 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par PREVIEW: MALAYSIA JUNE EXPORTS LIKELY UP 6.0% ON YEAR \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The year-on-year growth in Malaysia's exports likely remained weak in June as commodity prices eased while demand from advanced economies slowed, economists say. (published 0419 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 EQUITIES:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: MACARTHUR COAL CEO SAYS PEABODY, ARCELOR BID NOT HOSTILE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Macarthur Coal Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Tuesday it doesn't consider the A$4.7 billion takeover bid by \f28 \uc2 \f2 Peabody Energy Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . and \f28 \uc2 \f2 ArcelorMittal\f28 \uc2 \f2  to be hostile and will continue discussions with the companies and other parties that could lead to a higher bid. (published 0044 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par 2ND UPDATE: KIRIN TO BUY STAKE IN BRAZIL'S SCHINCARIOL FOR $2.56 BILLION \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Hampered by limited prospects at home and getting a good tailwind from the yen's rise, Kirin Holdings Co. said Tuesday it will spend about $2.56 billion to buy a majority stake in Schincariol, Brazil's second biggest brewer, in bid to quench its thirst in a market rich with growth potential. (published 0521 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par TOYOTA EKES OUT 1Q PROFIT DESPITE QUAKE, YEN; UPS FY OUTLOOK ON 2H REBOUND \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Toyota Motor Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Tuesday that it managed to squeeze out a profit in the April-June quarter and raised its fiscal-year net profit target by nearly 40%, despite the March 11 earthquake hampering production and the yen's surge denting its competitive edge overseas. (published 0621 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par ASAHI GROUP HOLDINGS 1H NET PROFIT UP 4.7% ON LOWER COSTS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Asahi Group Holdings Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Tuesday that its net profit for the interim period ended June 30 grew 4.7% from the previous year, in part due to lower expenses. (published 0627 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 SUMITOMO CORP\f28 \uc2 \f2  APR-JUN GROUP NET PROFIT UP 39% ON SOLID RESOURCE, REAL ESTATE PERFORMANCE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Sumitomo Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Tuesday that its net profit for the three months through June rose 39% on solid results in its natural resource, chemical and real estate businesses. (published 0501 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par MITSUI 1Q GROUP NET PROFIT Y132.70B, UP 29.4% ON YR \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Mitsui & Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Tuesday that its net profit for the three months through June rose 29% on dividends from the Sakhalin II natural gas project in eastern Russia and proceeds from sales of its shareholdings. (published 0455 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 FUJI HEAVY INDUSTRIES\f28 \uc2 \f2  1Q NET PROFIT SOARS ON HQ BUILDING SALE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Fuji Heavy Industries Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Tuesday that its net profit soared nearly 50% in the April-June quarter despite weaker sales, as it booked an extraordinary profit from the sale of an office building in Tokyo. (published 0428 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par RENESAS ELECTRONICS APR-JUN GROUP NET LOSS Y33.22B \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Renesas Electronics Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Tuesday that its net loss for the three months through June slightly deepened from the same quarter a year earlier, as the March 11 earthquake forced its key chip manufacturing plant to shut. (published 0637 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par HON HAI: INCREASE IN AUTOMATION TO RELEASE WORKERS FOR OTHER VALUE-ADDED TASKS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Hon Hai Precision Industry Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Tuesday it plans to increase automation on dangerous and monotonous tasks and to migrate more of its workers to value-added jobs such as product research and development, as part of the company's effort to improve its work environment following a spate of suicides at its plants across China over the past year. (published 0513 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: LIVINGSOCIAL PUSHES ASIA EXPANSION WITH BUY OF SOUTH KOREA'S TICKET MONSTER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Online deals company \f28 \uc2 \f2 LivingSocial\f28 \uc2 \f2  said Tuesday it will buy South Korea's largest daily deals site, Ticket Monster Inc., giving it a major beachhead in a key Asian country. (published 0443 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par HTC FILES APPEAL AGAINST US RULING FAVORING APPLE IN S3 GRAPHICS PATENT CLAIM \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 HTC Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . is appealing a U.S. International Trade Commission preliminary ruling declaring some \f28 \uc2 \f2 Apple Inc\f28 \uc2 \f2 . mobile products didn't violate patents held by S3 Graphics, HTC said in a statement Sunday. (published 0349 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par YANZHOU COAL: TO BUY AUSTRALIA COAL PRODUCTION ASSETS FOR A$202.5 MLN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Yanzhou Coal Mining Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Monday it has agreed to buy thermal coal exploration and production assets in Australia's Queensland state for A$202.5 million. (published 0021 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 TATA MOTORS\f28 \uc2 \f2  EXECUTIVE: TO REJIG DEALERSHIP NETWORK TO BOOST SALES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Tata Motors Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . is planning to restructure its local dealership network for its passenger vehicles this year in a bid to boost sales, a senior executive said Tuesday. (published 0659 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par HOUSING DEVELOPMENT FINANCE CEO: MAY RAISE LENDING RATES THIS WEEK \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Housing Development Finance Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . may raise its lending rates this week to pass on higher cost on funds to customers, the Indian mortgage lender's chief executive said Tuesday. (published 0603 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par KASIKORNBANK: 2011 LENDING GROWTH MAY EXCEED 7%-9% TARGET \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Thailand's \f28 \uc2 \f2 Kasikornbank PCL\f28 \uc2 \f2  said Tuesday its lending growth this year may breach its 7%-9% target after recording a robust growth of 8% in the six months ended June 30. (published 0555 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: PLDT 2ND-QUARTER NET PROFIT UP 3% AT PHP10.57 BLN ON LOWER TAXES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Philippine Long Distance Telephone Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 ., the country's largest telecommunications group by sales, said Tuesday its second-quarter net profit rose just 3% from a year earlier, with tighter controls on spending and a lower provision for income tax more than offsetting a decline in revenue. (published 0544 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: ASIAN SHARES FALL ON GROWTH WORRIES; STRONG YEN HITS NIKKEI \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Asian shares were mostly lower Tuesday as fresh worries over the global growth outlook offset relief over an 11th-hour deal to raise the U.S. debt ceiling, with stocks in Tokyo weighed by a strong yen. (published 0509 GMT) [ 02-08-11 0712GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ENERGY/COMMODITIES:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CHINA MAY TIGHTEN RARE EARTH EXPORT CONTROLS TO FIX LOOPHOLES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China may further tighten regulations on rare earth exports amid fears that sharply higher prices have led to a surge in rare earth smuggling and the export of byproducts that are not included in current quota restrictions. (published 0411 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par TAIWAN GOVERNMENT OFFICIAL: FORMOSA CLOSURE COULD PROMPT ANOTHER GDP REVISION \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Taiwan's economic growth will likely be hit by the partial shutdown of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Formosa Plastics Group\f28 \uc2 \f2 's major petrochemical complex in southern Taiwan and the company's declaration of force majeure on oil-product exports, although easing concerns on the U.S. debt situation will help cushion some of the shock, a government official said Tuesday. (published 0551 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 BARRICK GOLD\f28 \uc2 \f2  REMAINS BULLISH ON GOLD, COPPER PRICES -EXECUTIVE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Barrick Gold Ltd. remains bullish on the outlook for gold prices and expects prices for copper to remain well supported for several years due to rising demand, a regional executive for the world's largest gold producer said Tuesday. (published 0204 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par INDIA NUCLEAR PLANT OPERATOR SAYS 4 WORKERS EXPOSED TO LOW RADIATION \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Four workers at an atomic power station in western India were exposed to low levels of radiation on May 30 as radioactive material was "inadvertently" released into a spent-fuel duct, the station's operator said. (published 0632 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par S KOREA TO ADD 4 FOOD ITEMS TO TARIFF-CUT LIST \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The South Korean government will add four new food items to its list of imports eligible for tariff cuts to help stabilize consumer prices, the Ministry of Strategy and Finance said Tuesday. (published 0100 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par PETROVIETNAM LAUNCHES 2011 LICENSING ROUND FOR 9 OFFSHORE BLOCKS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 State-run \f28 \uc2 \f2 Vietnam Oil and Gas Group\f28 \uc2 \f2 , or \f28 \uc2 \f2 PetroVietnam\f28 \uc2 \f2 , said Tuesday that it has launched a licensing round for nine offshore blocks for this year. (published 0326 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par INTERVIEW: ANGLOGOLD HAS POTENTIAL TO SHARPLY BOOST AUSTRALIA OUTPUT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 AngloGold Ashanti Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 ., one of the world's largest gold producers, may produce as much as 700,000 troy ounces a year in Australia as it develops a promising new mine and goes underground at its existing Sunrise Dam \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operation\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , \f28 \uc2 \f2 Graham Ehm\f28 \uc2 \f2 , vice president for Australasia, said Tuesday. (published 0544 GMT) [ 02-08-11 0712GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 62550   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020110802e782000kx\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2