ess pronounced. Equinet also expects unfavorable comparables and negative \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  effects to have hampered growth in 2Q.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Fresnillo PLC\f28 \uc2 \f2  (FRES.LN): 1H Earnings \par Due: August 2 at 0600 GMT \par Company Survey of 6 Analysts \par Average 1H Revenue: $1.09B, up 80% ($605.7M in 1H 2010) \par Average 1H Ebitda: $812.6M ($392M in 1H 2010) \par Average 1H EPS: $0.657 ($0.308 in 1H 2010) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Note: EPS is forecast to more than double, largely due to higher gold and silver prices. Analysts will seek an update on the company's outlook for 2H and concerns on how cost inflation is affecting the business. \f28 \uc2 \f2 Deutsche Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2  also says it will seek an update on start-up unit operating costs for the newly commissioned Saucito mine. \f28 \uc2 \f2 Fresnillo\f28 \uc2 \f2  is targeting full year output of 44M ounces of silver and 400,000 ounces of attributable gold output.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Metro AG\f28 \uc2 \f2  (MEO.XE): 2Q Earnings \par Due: Aug. 2 at 0515 GMT \par DJ Survey of 6 Analysts \par Average adjusted EBIT: EUR340M, up 1.8% (EUR334M in 2Q10) \par Average Net Profit: EUR80M, up 82% (EUR44M in 2Q10) \par Average Sales: EUR15.78B, up 0.4% (EUR15.71B in 2Q10) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Note: Analysts expect Metro's 2Q numbers to be mixed. On July 26, Metro said it expects the Media Markt and Saturn units to be hit in 2Q, therefore, diminishing the negative surprise potential of the 2Q results, Warburg says. However, analysts expect Cash & Carry, Real and \f28 \uc2 \f2 Kaufhof\f28 \uc2 \f2  businesses to show positive Easter effects. Any details about the new online business strategy and integration of the internet business with the electronics unit would be interesting, analysts say. Meanwhile, the company has lowered its 2011 sales outlook, but confirmed its EBIT expectations for the year.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Titan Cement\f28 \uc2 \f2  (TITK.AT): 2Q Earnings \par Due: Aug. 2, approx 1430 GMT \par DJ Survey of 5 Analysts \par Average Revenue:    EUR328M, -17% (EUR394.8M in 2Q 2010) \par Average Ebitda:     EUR67M,  -33% (EUR100.2M in 2Q 2010) \par Average Net Profit: EUR16M,  -63% (EUR43.5M in 2Q 2010) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Note: Ongoing weakness in key Greek and US markets continue to weigh on earnings, while south-east Europe \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  seen flat. Relative organic strength in Turkey and Egypt may be offset by \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  losses in local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . Market will focus on outlook for Greek, US markets.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Wacker Chemie\f28 \uc2 \f2  (WCH.XE): 2Q Earnings \par Due: Aug. 2 at 0515 GMT \par DJ Survey of 8 Analysts \par Average Net Profit:EUR154M,  +13%  (EUR135M in 2Q 2010) \par Average Revenue:   EUR1.33B, +11%  (EUR1.20B in 2Q 2010) \par Average Ebitda:    EUR337M,  +9.1% (EUR309M in 2Q 2010) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Note: Analysts expect a rise in sales and profit but rising raw material expenses and unfavorable \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rates should nevertheless weigh on results. \f28 \uc2 \f2 HSBC\f28 \uc2 \f2  expects Chemicals to grow 8% quarter-on-quarter driven by seasonal stronger demand and higher prices in Polymers, but it sees lower momentum compared to previous years given slow construction activity in mature markets. Focus will also be on 2H outlook in Siltronic and potential wafer price increases given weakening demand and following inventory build in 1H.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Xstrata PLC\f28 \uc2 \f2  (XTA.LN): 1H Earnings \par Due: August 2 at 0600 GMT \par Company Survey of 16 Analysts \par Average 1H Underlying Ebitda: $5.84B, up 30% ($4.49B in 1H 2010) \par Average 1H Underlying Net Profit Attributable \par To Shareholders: $2.92B, up 27% ($2.30B in 1H 2010) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Note: Underlying net profit seen up due to higher achieved commodity prices which are forecast to offset lackluster production figures. Analysts are focusing on the company's massive growth pipeline and whether cost inflation and the strength of emerging-market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  are likely to result in higher project costs or project delays. Analysts will also seek an update on the potential for a special dividend and on M&A, particularly in a tie-up with \f28 \uc2 \f2 Glencore\f28 \uc2 \f2  which owns a 34.5% stake in \f28 \uc2 \f2 Xstrata\f28 \uc2 \f2 . [ 02-08-11 0501GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Absa Group (ASA.JO)  : Interim 2011 Results presentation \par Absa Group (ASA.JO) : Interim 2011 Results \par Affecto Oyj (AFE1V.HE) : Q2 2011 Press & analyst briefing \par \f28 \uc2 \f2 Affecto Oyj\f28 \uc2 \f2  (AFE1V.HE) : Q2 2011 Results \par Alapis (ALAPIS.AT) : EGM \par ALITA AB : EGM \par \f28 \uc2 \f2 Arkema\f28 \uc2 \f2  (AKE.FR) : Interim 2011 Results \par \f28 \uc2 \f2 Atlantia Spa\f28 \uc2 \f2  (ATL.MI) : Interim 2011 Results \par Avangard (AVGR.LN) : Interim 2011 Results \par \f28 \uc2 \f2 Banco Espirito Santo\f28 \uc2 \f2  SpA (BES.LB) : Interim 2011 Earnings conference call \par Bankas Snoras (SRS1L.LV) : Interim 2011 Results \par \f28 \uc2 \f2 Barclays\f28 \uc2 \f2   (BARC.LN) : Interim 2011 Webcast \par Bezeq Israel Telecom (BEZQ.TV) : Q2 2011 Earnings conference call / Webcast \par Bezeq Israel Telecom (BEZQ.TV) : Q2 2011 Results \par Biotech Growth Trust (The) (BIOG.LN) : Interim Management Statement \par BlackRock Latin American Investment Trust (BRLA.LN) : Interim 2011 Results \par BMW AG (\f28 \uc2 \f2 BMW.XE\f28 \uc2 \f2 ) : Q2 2011 Earnings conference call \par \f28 \uc2 \f2 BNP Paribas SA\f28 \uc2 \f2  (BNP.FR) : Q2 2011 Webcast \par Caffyns (CFYN.LN) : Interim Management Statement \par Caja de ahorros del Mediterraneo (CAM.MC) : Q2 2011 Results \par Capita