\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Swiss franc buoyant, yen restrained by  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  threat\b0\par\par\uc2 796 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 August 2011\par 13:40\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Swiss franc holds firm even as U.S. debt deal looks set\par \par \uc2 * Worries about global economy growing after weak data\par \par \uc2 * Wariness on BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  limits dollar's falls vs yen\par \par \uc2 * Speculators take dollar long positions on chance of BOJ move\par \par \uc2 By Ian Chua and Chikafumi Hodo\par \par \uc2 TOKYO/SYDNEY, Aug 2 (Reuters) - The safe-haven Swiss franc gained on Tuesday on worries about the global economy even as the U.S. looked to have averted a debt default after the House of Representatives approved an 11th hour deal to raise the government's borrowing limit.\par \par \uc2 Strength in the yen also drew more warnings from Japanese officials about possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and nudged the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  closer to a further easing in policy.\par \par \uc2 The U.S. debt bill will now need to clear the Senate, which is expected to approve the $2.1 trillion deficit-cutting plan.\par \par \uc2 "While the political cloud of uncertainty may lift somewhat, the economic storm clouds are darkening," Yelena Shulyatyeva, an economist at \uc2 BNP Paribas\uc2  wrote in a client note.\par \par \uc2 The Swiss franc held near record highs against the euro and dollar, having risen strongly overnight after reports on Monday showed the world's manufacturing sector expanded at its weakest pace in two years last month. .\par \par \uc2 "Clearly, the report raises worries that the sector, which has been a key engine of growth during the current recovery, is losing steam reflecting a weakening around the globe in manufacturing," Shulyatyeva said.\par \par \uc2 The dollar inched down 0.1 percent to 0.7830 Swiss francs\par \par \uc2 , having plumbed an all-time low around 0.7730 overnight. The euro traded at 1.1173 francs , not far off a record low near 1.1025.\par \par \uc2 The dollar rose 0.4 percent to 77.49 yen having set a four-month low of 76.29 yen the previous day on EBS, close to its record low of 76.25 yen hit after the March 11 earthquake.\par \par \uc2 Masanari Takada, a \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Nomura Securities, said there is a chance Japanese authorities could \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  should the dollar approach its all-time low, a level where a slew of option-related sell orders are rumoured to be placed.\par \par \uc2 "Coupled with the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's monetary measures, \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  will be able to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to push up the dollar against the yen," Takada said.\par \par \uc2 "Still, it may be difficult to keep the dollar bolstered for long as it is under downward pressure because of caution towards the outlook for the U.S. economy and falling in U.S. Treasury yields," he said.\par \par \uc2 Sellers backed off due to caution over possible yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by Japanese authorities.\par \par \uc2 Finance Minster Yoshihiko Noda said he was closely communicating with the Bank of Japan and other countries on how to address the yen's recent rise.\par \par \uc2 "If the strong yen continues, it will unmistakably impact some industries. I want to closely analyse the potential impact," Noda told reporters after a cabinet meeting.\par \par \uc2 The dollar drew demand from speculators who were detected building up dollar long positions in an anticipation of possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Tokyo dealers said.\par \par \uc2 A series of stop-loss buy orders was cited at 77.70-78.20 yen, but Japanese exporters were expected to sell strongly between 79 and 80 yen, dealers said.\par \par \uc2 Tension over \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  would increase should the dollar dip below 77 yen, with stop-loss sell orders rumoured at 76.80 yen and major stops around 76.25 yen and 76.10 yen, they said.\par \par \uc2 Sources familiar with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's thinking said it is expected to ease monetary policy this week to support a fragile economic recovery if the yen continues to rise quickly enough to trigger \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "\b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is really only successful when it's coordinated and I can't see central banks getting together in the current environment to do a coordinated \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken the yen," said Joseph Capurso, a strategist at Commonwealth Bank in Sydney.\par \par \uc2 The dollar managed to hang on to most of the gains it made overnight against the euro, which is hampered by the euro zone debt problems.\par \par \uc2 The euro was at $1.4265 , still near two-week lows around $1.4184 plumbed overnight.\par \par \uc2 The Australian dollar bounced back from the previous day's low to last stand at $1.0980 .\par \par \uc2 The Aussie's immediate outlook depends on the \uc2 Reserve Bank of Australia\uc2 's interest rate decision due at 0430 GMT. Analysts polled by Reuters on Friday generally expected no change to the 4.75 percent cash rate, but some called for a hike to 5.00 percent.\par \par \uc2 (Additional reporting by Masayuki Kitano in Singapore and Hideyuki Sano in Tokyo; Editing by Michael Watson)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 1)   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020110804e7810010v\par }\page {\par\fs20{\