\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 3-Sudden US dollar rise vs yen leaves market wary\b0\par\par\uc2 745 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 August 2011\par 18:37\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Traders cite options structures at 75-yen level\par \par \uc2 * Nikkei reports \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  preparing to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 * One-month implied volatilities in dollar/yen remain low\par \par \uc2 (Adds details, quote, byline)\par \par \uc2 By Gertrude Chavez-Dreyfuss\par \par \uc2 NEW YORK, Aug 1 (Reuters) - The \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market was on high alert on Monday for signs of action from Japanese monetary authorities to weaken the yen after a huge bank order to buy U.S. dollars raised eyebrows.\par \par \uc2 Traders said the move did not appear to be \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  but the timing of the brief spike in the dollar, coming as it did after it neared a record low versus the yen, left the market jittery.\par \par \uc2 An official from the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Tokyo said the office was aware of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  movements but he could not comment on the dollar's sudden rise versus the yen.\par \par \uc2 On Monday, Japan's Nikkei newspaper said, without citing sources, that the Japanese government is preparing to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to weaken the yen as it nears a record high against the dollar. The report also said the Bank of Japan has begun discussing additional monetary easing. For more, click on [ID:nN1E77015H].\par \par \uc2 If Japanese officials were to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken the yen, recent history suggests the lows struck by the dollar on Monday could be the place. It's where \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  with the help of other developed nations back in March.\par \par \uc2 It also explains why the market is on edge, though some analysts say conditions now are different from the situation in March. Back then the international financial community banded together to help Japan's economy shortly after its earthquake and tsunami disaster.\par \par \uc2 "The talk was that there was a huge order from a large Japanese bank, but it was part of the normal flow of the market," said a London-based trader.\par \par \uc2 Two traders cited talk that named Nomura as that big Japanese bank which bought the dollar against the yen. Nomura's corporate communications office in New York declined to comment on the speculation.\par \par \uc2 The dollar surged as high as 77.100 yen <JPY=EBS> on trading platform EBS from 76.456 within one minute. It was last at 77.160 yen, up 0.6 percent on the day.\par \par \uc2 The dollar had earlier plunged to 76.290 yen, its weakest since the mid-March \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken the surging yen. The all-time low was 76.250 hit on March 17.\par \par \uc2 "There is no indication that there was \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , no rumor, no nothing. There wasn't even anything about the Bank of Japan checking rates," said a trader from a U.S. bank.\par \par \uc2 Despite losses in dollar/yen, one-month volatility in the pair remained subdued at 10.65 percent on Monday <JPY1MO=>, suggesting the pair's decline has so far been orderly. Prior to the coordinated \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in March, volatility was at 20.94 percent.\par \par \uc2 The dollar's slump against the yen came amid a protracted slide by the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  during weeks of tense negotiations in Washington over raising the national debt limit to avert a catostrophic default.\par \par \uc2 The yen, along with the Swiss franc, has been one of the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market's favorite safe havens from recent U.S. budget turmoil.\par \par \uc2 Another trader said there are numerous options structures at the 75 yen level.\par \par \uc2 Richard Franulovich, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at \uc2 Westpac\uc2  in New York said if there is indeed a 75 yen-options structure, that suggests the market could see another wave of dollar selling against the yen if that level is triggered.\par \par \uc2 "A lot of Japanese retail investors who have bought a lot of Aussie/yen lately could be capitulating and we could see dollar/yen get to 70 quite quickly," he said.\par \par \uc2 Oddly, it has come as Japanese domestic investors have built up short yen positions designed to take advantage of higher yielding investments overseas.\par \par \uc2 Traders' net long position in the dollar versus the yen \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  pair and other yen crosses hit a record of 722.3 billion yen two weeks ago or around $9.4 billion, according to data from the Tokyo Financial Exchange. Dollar/yen net long bets from these investors totaled 275.4 billion yen, or roughly $3.8 billion.\par \par \uc2 Prior to the coordinated \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in March, Japanese margin traders had also built up significant long positions in dollar/yen.\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2 /JAPAN (UPDATE 3)   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020110801e781001gd\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
