\par\par \b \uc2 WORLD  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 : Dlr Pares Gains Vs Yen After US Debt Deal Bounce\b0\par\par\uc2 701 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 August 2011\par 07:18\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 -- Dollar jumps vs the yen on U.S. debt ceiling deal, falls back on continued ratings concern.\par \par \uc2 -- Deal calls for increasing debt ceiling by at least $2.1 trillion, uncertainties remain over scale of savings measures.\par \par \uc2 -- While praising progress on the U.S. impasse, Japan finance minister indicates continued caution over yen strength.\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    By Andrew Monahan and Enda Curran \par    Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 TOKYO (Dow Jones)--A framework agreement in the long-running debt ceiling battle in Washington sent the dollar up briefly against the yen Monday morning in Asia, but the greenback's gains faded on continued concern over a possible U.S. sovereign downgrade and further economic softening.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Analysts say they expect the U.S. to avoid default despite both Democratic and Republican leaders describing the agreement as less than ideal. The framework calls for increasing the debt ceiling by at least $2.1 trillion through the end of 2012 and for $2.4 trillion in deficit reduction measures.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Remaining uncertainties in the exact parameters, with House Republicans and the White House releasing different figures for the expected savings, are tempering dollar gains, analysts said. That the deal came only shortly before a Tuesday deadline also keeps ratings concerns in play, they said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "It's very possible that the U.S. could still lose its AAA sovereign rating," said Richard Grace, chief \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist at \f28 \uc2 \f2 Commonwealth Bank of Australia\f28 \uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 While Japanese Finance Minister Yoshihiko Noda praised the progress on the U.S. impasse, he said he would continue to "closely watch" the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Some analysts said the Japanese finance ministry could yet step in to sell the yen, even if the U.S. deal had diminished the chances of immediate action.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Ministry of Finance\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is looking at \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  from the standpoint of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's long-term competitiveness," said Osamu Takashima, chief \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist at Citibank Japan. Any future retreat in Japanese equities could increase pressure on Tokyo to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , Takashima said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Traders said the Bank of Korea and the Philippine \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  had \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  earlier Monday to stem rises in their \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  against the U.S. unit.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The dollar's failure to hold its gains Monday came also as investors had already priced in expectations for default to be averted.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "It was just political theater, and the focus will now shift back to more fundamental problems for the dollar, such as low interest rates," said Tohru Sasaki, chief \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist at \f28 \uc2 \f2 JP Morgan\f28 \uc2 \f2  in Japan.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 At 0450 GMT, the dollar was at Y77.55, up from Y76.78 late Friday in New York, but down from the high it hit at Y78.05 after the deal was announced.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The euro was at Y111.58 compared with Y110.05, and at $1.4389 from $1.4391.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The ICE Dollar Index was at 73.855 from 73.750.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Key for the dollar later this week is the U.S. non-farm payrolls report for July Friday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Interbank \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Foreign Exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Rates At 1250 EDT / 0450 GMT \par  \par                          Latest     Previous   %Chg   Daily   Daily    %Chg \par                                     2150 GMT          High    Low      12/31 \par Dollar Rates \par  \par  \par USD/JPY Japan            77.54-56       77.16-24  +0.45    78.04    77.14  -4.40 \par EUR/USD Euro            1.4387-90      1.4383-84  +0.04   1.4402   1.4348  +7.45 \par GBP/USD U.K.            1.6443-48      1.6424-30  +0.11   1.6474   1.6390  +5.37 \par USD/CHF Switzerland     0.7927-30      0.7911-32  +0.09   0.7952   0.7906 -15.20 \par USD/CAD Canada          0.9522-26      0.9553-56  -0.32   0.9557   0.9508  -4.26 \par AUD/USD Australia       1.1040-44      1.0986-88  +0.50   1.1060   1.0988  +7.90 \par NZD/USD New Zealand     0.8819-24      0.8789-92  +0.35   0.8842   0.8788 +13.15 \par  \par Euro Rates \par  \par EUR/JPY Japan           111.56-60      110.78-01  +0.56   112.24   110.74  +2.71 \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Andrew Monahan and Enda Curran, Dow Jones Newswires; +813-6269-2785; andrew.monahan@dowjones.com [ 01-08-11 0518GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1034 1863 28038 4162   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020110801e781000c7\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
