\par\par \b \uc2 MARKET TALK: US Deal Doesn't Preclude JPY  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  - Citi\b0\par\par\uc2 195 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 August 2011\par 03:50\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 0150 GMT [Dow Jones] While the U.S. debt ceiling deal makes Japanese JPY-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  unlikely for now, as the agreement has kicked Japanese share prices higher, the longer-term possibility of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  "is larger than the market expects," says Osamu Takashima, chief \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Citibank \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 . "The \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  is looking at \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the standpoint of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's long-term competitiveness, including points such as Japanese firms' ability to compete with Korean competitors with the yen strong against the won." If the country's Nikkei Stock Average begins falling again in coming weeks, that would be one possible trigger for Tokyo to step into the \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, Takashima says. He adds that given its longer-term focus, the government is likely now more concerned over sustained JPY strength, rather than on smoothing out any sudden moves in the unit. The USD/JPY is at 77.84, off an earlier session high of 78.05. (andrew.monahan@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in Singapore. 65 64154 140; MarketTalk@dowjones.com \par  \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 [ 01-08-11 0150GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1012 1037 1085 5011 55117 75112   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020110801e7810003u\par }\par \b \uc2 Zusammenfassung der Suche\b0\par \par  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\